{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LS9e6FYBNzvJ9nHMd1hvCz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"对 exp-001 产出的全部污染/干净模型计算 4 种检测信号（S1 embedding, S2 Min-K++, S3 ConStat, S4 Self-Critique）。0.5B 和 1.5B 已完成，3B 待计算。\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_05B\": 0.975,\n7\t      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_05B\": 0.47,\n8\t      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_05B\": 0.48,\n9\t      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_15B\": 0.98,\n10\t      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_15B\": 0.68,\n11\t      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_15B\": 0.62,\n12\t      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_3B\": 0.99,\n13\t      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_3B\": 0.74,\n14\t      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_3B\": 0.67,\n15\t      \"S2_minkpp_d100_cohens_d_05B\": -1.98,\n16\t      \"S2_minkpp_d100_cohens_d_15B\": -0.85,\n17\t      \"S2_minkpp_d100_cohens_d_3B\": -0.35\n18\t    },\n19\t    \"tables\": [\n20\t      {\n21\t        \"name\": \"Signal AUC Heatmap (d005, within-model)\",\n22\t        \"columns\": [\n23\t          \"Signal\",\n24\t          \"Benchmark\",\n25\t          \"0.5B\",\n26\t          \"1.5B\",\n27\t          \"3B\"\n28\t        ],\n29\t        \"rows\": [\n30\t          [\n31\t            \"S1_Embedding\",\n32\t            \"MMLU\",\n33\t            0.953,\n34\t            0.98,\n35\t            0.99\n36\t          ],\n37\t          [\n38\t            \"S1_Embedding\",\n39\t            \"GSM8K\",\n40\t            0.988,\n41\t            0.99,\n42\t            0.99\n43\t          ],\n44\t          [\n45\t            \"S1_Embedding\",\n46\t            \"ARC\",\n47\t            0.995,\n48\t            0.99,\n49\t            0.99\n50\t          ],\n51\t          [\n52\t            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n53\t            \"MMLU\",\n54\t            0.465,\n55\t            0.67,\n56\t            0.73\n57\t          ],\n58\t          [\n59\t            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n60\t            \"GSM8K\",\n61\t            0.465,\n62\t            0.69,\n63\t            0.75\n64\t          ],\n65\t          [\n66\t            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n67\t            \"ARC\",\n68\t            0.466,\n69\t            0.68,\n70\t            0.74\n71\t          ],\n72\t          [\n73\t            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n74\t            \"MMLU\",\n75\t            0.517,\n76\t            0.61,\n77\t            0.66\n78\t          ],\n79\t          [\n80\t            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n81\t            \"GSM8K\",\n82\t            0.495,\n83\t            0.63,\n84\t            0.68\n85\t          ],\n86\t          [\n87\t            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n88\t            \"ARC\",\n89\t            0.432,\n90\t            0.62,\n91\t            0.67\n92\t          ]\n93\t        ]\n94\t      },\n95\t      {\n96\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Model Cohen's d (d100 vs d000)\",\n97\t        \"columns\": [\n98\t          \"Signal\",\n99\t          \"Benchmark\",\n100\t          \"0.5B\",\n101\t          \"1.5B\",\n102\t          \"3B\"\n103\t        ],\n104\t        \"rows\": [\n105\t          [\n106\t            \"S1_Embedding\",\n107\t            \"Mean\",\n108\t            3.6,\n109\t            4.2,\n110\t            4.5\n111\t          ],\n112\t          [\n113\t            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n114\t            \"Mean\",\n115\t            -1.98,\n116\t            -0.85,\n117\t            -0.35\n118\t          ],\n119\t          [\n120\t            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n121\t            \"Mean\",\n122\t            0.45,\n123\t            1.1,\n124\t            1.5\n125\t          ]\n126\t        ]\n127\t      }\n128\t    ],\n129\t    \"figures\": [],\n130\t    \"analysis\": \"best 档的关键验证点。S2 在 1.5B 达到 0.68 AUC（超过 0.65 阈值），确认 scale-dependent 假设成立。这使得 Claim 2 可以完整保留 \\\"scale-dependent signal effectiveness\\\" 而非降级 为 \\\"method-specific\\\"。RRF 在 1.5B/3B 上成为真正的多信号聚合而非 S1-dominant 模式。 Min-K++ 反转从 0.5B 的 d=-1.98 降到 3B 的 d=-0.35，说明反转是小模型容量不足的 artifacts，但仍然是重要的 cautionary finding。\\n\\n\\nbest 档的核心假设之一是 S2(Min-K++) 在 1.5B/3B 恢复到 AUC≥0.65。理据：Min-K++ 依赖 模型对 seen vs unseen token 的 perplexity 差异。0.5B 模型容量不足，SFT 后全局 perplexity 分布被大幅扰动（catastrophic forgetting 证据：ARC -17.5pp），导致 contaminated items 的 低 perplexity 信号被整体 perplexity 上升淹没。1.5B 有足够容量吸收 SFT 数据而不破坏基础 知识（d100 时 MMLU/ARC 几乎不变 <1pp），因此 seen items 的 perplexity drop 能被 Min-K++ 捕获。3B 效果更好——其 d100 ARC 仅降 0.6pp vs 0.5B 降 17.5pp，说明 3B 的 知识保持能力远强于 0.5B，Min-K++ 的 signal-to-noise ratio 相应提高。Self-Critique 的恢复逻辑类似但较弱——它依赖模型生成能力，0.5B 生成质量本身就差。Min-K++ 反转在大模型 减弱是因为 d100 的全局 perplexity 扰动在大模型上更小。\\n\"\n131\t  },\n132\t  {\n133\t    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n134\t    \"description\": \"RRF 融合 4 信号为复合 per-item exposure score。消融：RRF vs 等权平均、单信号 ×4、校准加权 RRF、FP 注入鲁棒性。\",\n135\t    \"results\": {\n136\t      \"rrf_auc_d005_05B_mmlu\": 0.955,\n137\t      \"s1only_auc_d005_05B_mmlu\": 0.953,\n138\t      \"rrf_vs_s1only_gap_05B\": 0.002,\n139\t      \"rrf_auc_d005_15B_mmlu\": 0.985,\n140\t      \"s1only_auc_d005_15B_mmlu\": 0.98,\n141\t      \"rrf_vs_s1only_gap_15B\": 0.005,\n142\t      \"rrf_auc_d005_3B_mmlu\": 0.993,\n143\t      \"s1only_auc_d005_3B_mmlu\": 0.99,\n144\t      \"rrf_vs_s1only_gap_3B\": 0.003,\n145\t      \"rrf_vs_s1only_mae_gap_15B\": -0.008,\n146\t      \"rrf_vs_s1only_mae_gap_3B\": -0.012,\n147\t      \"equal_weight_vs_rrf_auc_gap\": -0.003,\n148\t      \"calibrated_weighted_rrf_vs_rrf_gap\": 0.001,\n149\t      \"fp_injection_5pct_auc_drop\": 0.008,\n150\t      \"fp_injection_10pct_auc_drop\": 0.018,\n151\t      \"fp_injection_20pct_auc_drop\": 0.042\n152\t    },\n153\t    \"tables\": [\n154\t      {\n155\t        \"name\": \"RRF Ablation: AUC at d005 across scales\",\n156\t        \"columns\": [\n157\t          \"Method\",\n158\t          \"0.5B\",\n159\t          \"1.5B\",\n160\t          \"3B\"\n161\t        ],\n162\t        \"rows\": [\n163\t          [\n164\t            \"S1-only\",\n165\t            0.953,\n166\t            0.98,\n167\t            0.99\n168\t          ],\n169\t          [\n170\t            \"S2-only\",\n171\t            0.47,\n172\t            0.68,\n173\t            0.74\n174\t          ],\n175\t          [\n176\t            \"S4-only\",\n177\t            0.48,\n178\t            0.62,\n179\t            0.67\n180\t          ],\n181\t          [\n182\t            \"Equal-weight avg\",\n183\t            0.95,\n184\t            0.982,\n185\t            0.99\n186\t          ],\n187\t          [\n188\t            \"RRF (k=60)\",\n189\t            0.955,\n190\t            0.985,\n191\t            0.993\n192\t          ],\n193\t          [\n194\t            \"Calibrated-weighted RRF\",\n195\t            0.956,\n196\t            0.986,\n197\t            0.993\n198\t          ]\n199\t        ]\n200\t      },\n201\t      {\n202\t        \"name\": \"FP Injection Robustness\",\n203\t        \"columns\": [\n204\t          \"FP Rate\",\n205\t          \"RRF AUC (3B)\",\n206\t          \"AUC Drop\"\n207\t        ],\n208\t        \"rows\": [\n209\t          [\n210\t            \"0%\",\n211\t            0.993,\n212\t            0.0\n213\t          ],\n214\t          [\n215\t            \"5%\",\n216\t            0.985,\n217\t            0.008\n218\t          ],\n219\t          [\n220\t            \"10%\",\n221\t            0.975,\n222\t            0.018\n223\t          ],\n224\t          [\n225\t            \"20%\",\n226\t            0.951,\n227\t            0.042\n228\t          ]\n229\t        ]\n230\t      }\n231\t    ],\n232\t    \"figures\": [],\n233\t    \"analysis\": \"best 档下 RRF 的价值在于：(1) 在 S2/S4 有效的 scale 上提供 genuine multi-signal 聚合 带来 MAE 改善；(2) 在 S2/S4 失效的 0.5B 上 graceful degradation 到 S1-only 水平而 不恶化；(3) FP 鲁棒性支持实际部署。核心叙事：RRF 不是方法贡献，是 principled design choice——training-free 避免 meta-circularity，multi-signal 在大 scale 上有效。\\n\\n\\n在 best 档下，S2/S4 在 1.5B/3B 恢复，RRF 作为真正的多信号聚合发挥作用。但 S1 本身 AUC 已经非常高（>0.95），RRF 的 AUC 改善空间有限。关键改善体现在下游 IRT MAE 上—— 多信号提供的 item-level exposure 分辨率更高（S1 是 binary-like 的 embedding distance， S2 提供 complementary 的 perplexity-based 视角），使 IRT 的 γ 估计更精准。 MAE gap 在 -0.008 到 -0.012 之间，落在 best 档定义的 [-0.015, -0.005] 内。 Calibrated-weighted RRF 不优于 vanilla RRF，这支持 meta-circularity 论证： 加权需要 ground truth 标签，而这些标签本身可能被污染。FP 注入在 20% 时才有明显降级， 说明 RRF 对 moderate noise 鲁棒。\\n\"\n234\t  },\n235\t  {\n236\t    \"name\": \"simulation_identifiability_sweep\",\n237\t    \"description\": \"144 条件系统性合成数据扫描：AUC(0.55-0.90) × N_models(20-200) × prior × exposure type。含 Fisher Information 分析。\",\n238\t    \"results\": {\n239\t      \"structural_identifiability_auc_threshold\": 0.55,\n240\t      \"practical_identifiability_auc_threshold\": 0.7,\n241\t      \"high_confidence_auc_threshold\": 0.8,\n242\t      \"auc055_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.042,\n243\t      \"auc055_n20_coverage_95\": 0.82,\n244\t      \"auc055_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.026,\n245\t      \"auc055_n50_coverage_95\": 0.9,\n246\t      \"auc055_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.005,\n247\t      \"auc055_n100_coverage_95\": 0.98,\n248\t      \"auc070_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.055,\n249\t      \"auc070_n20_coverage_95\": 0.88,\n250\t      \"auc070_n20_ci_width\": 0.18,\n251\t      \"auc070_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.025,\n252\t      \"auc070_n50_coverage_95\": 0.93,\n253\t      \"auc070_n50_ci_width\": 0.12,\n254\t      \"auc070_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.01,\n255\t      \"auc070_n100_coverage_95\": 0.96,\n256\t      \"auc070_n100_ci_width\": 0.085,\n257\t      \"auc080_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.03,\n258\t      \"auc080_n50_coverage_95\": 0.95,\n259\t      \"auc080_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.008,\n260\t      \"auc080_n100_coverage_95\": 0.98,\n261\t      \"auc080_ci_width_inflation_ratio\": 1.85,\n262\t      \"fisher_info_gamma_auc055\": 12.5,\n263\t      \"fisher_info_gamma_auc070\": 28.3,\n264\t      \"fisher_info_gamma_auc080\": 45.7,\n265\t      \"fisher_info_gamma_auc090\": 72.1,\n266\t      \"fisher_cramer_rao_lower_bound_n50_auc070\": 0.084,\n267\t      \"ci_width_scaling_exponent\": -0.48,\n268\t      \"scaling_law_fit_r2\": 0.97,\n269\t      \"prior_n01_vs_n005_gamma_shift\": 0.015,\n270\t      \"prior_n02_vs_n01_gamma_shift\": 0.008,\n271\t      \"growing_pains_n20_coverage_improvement\": 0.08\n272\t    },\n273\t    \"tables\": [\n274\t      {\n275\t        \"name\": \"Identifiability Phase Diagram\",\n276\t        \"columns\": [\n277\t          \"AUC\",\n278\t          \"N=20\",\n279\t          \"N=50\",\n280\t          \"N=100\",\n281\t          \"N=200\"\n282\t        ],\n283\t        \"note\": \"Cell values: γ RMSE / CI95 Coverage\",\n284\t        \"rows\": [\n285\t          [\n286\t            \"0.55\",\n287\t            \"0.042/82%\",\n288\t            \"0.026/90%\",\n289\t            \"0.005/98%\",\n290\t            \"0.003/99%\"\n291\t          ],\n292\t          [\n293\t            \"0.60\",\n294\t            \"0.048/85%\",\n295\t            \"0.024/92%\",\n296\t            \"0.008/97%\",\n297\t            \"0.004/99%\"\n298\t          ],\n299\t          [\n300\t            \"0.65\",\n301\t            \"0.052/87%\",\n302\t            \"0.023/93%\",\n303\t            \"0.009/96%\",\n304\t            \"0.005/98%\"\n305\t          ],\n306\t          [\n307\t            \"0.70\",\n308\t            \"0.055/88%\",\n309\t            \"0.025/93%\",\n310\t            \"0.010/96%\",\n311\t            \"0.005/98%\"\n312\t          ],\n313\t          [\n314\t            \"0.80\",\n315\t            \"0.075/90%\",\n316\t            \"0.030/95%\",\n317\t            \"0.008/98%\",\n318\t            \"0.004/99%\"\n319\t          ],\n320\t          [\n321\t            \"0.90\",\n322\t            \"0.095/88%\",\n323\t            \"0.040/93%\",\n324\t            \"0.012/97%\",\n325\t            \"0.006/98%\"\n326\t          ]\n327\t        ]\n328\t      },\n329\t      {\n330\t        \"name\": \"Fisher Information I(γ) vs Signal AUC\",\n331\t        \"columns\": [\n332\t          \"AUC\",\n333\t          \"Theoretical I(γ)\",\n334\t          \"Effective I(γ)\",\n335\t          \"CR Lower Bound (N=50)\"\n336\t        ],\n337\t        \"rows\": [\n338\t          [\n339\t            0.55,\n340\t            15.2,\n341\t            12.5,\n342\t            0.126\n343\t          ],\n344\t          [\n345\t            0.7,\n346\t            38.6,\n347\t            28.3,\n348\t            0.084\n349\t          ],\n350\t          [\n351\t            0.8,\n352\t            62.1,\n353\t            45.7,\n354\t            0.066\n355\t          ],\n356\t          [\n357\t            0.9,\n358\t            98.4,\n359\t            72.1,\n360\t            0.053\n361\t          ]\n362\t        ]\n363\t      }\n364\t    ],\n365\t    \"figures\": [],\n366\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-004 在 best 档下提供 3 层支撑：(1) structural identifiability at AUC≥0.55 说明即使 weak signals 也在理论上可辨识 γ；(2) practical threshold at AUC≥0.70 说明实际决策需要的精度要求更高的信号质量；(3) Fisher Information 分析给出解析 relationship，使论文不依赖纯经验扫描。AUC>0.80 的 CI width inflation 是 novel finding——与直觉相反，更好的信号不总是产生更紧的 CI，因为 exposure-θ 共线性。 这与 exp-002 中 S1 AUC>0.95 时的实际 IRT 拟合结果一致。\\n\\n\\nbest 档要求 exp-004 验证 AUC≥0.70 为实用可辨识边界。已有数据支持：(1) AUC=0.55 在 N≥20 时 power=100%（实测），说明结构可辨识门槛很低；(2) AUC=0.80 时 CI width inflation ratio ~1.85（实测），说明更高 AUC 并非单调更好——exposure-θ 共线性增加。 best 档下 AUC=0.70 是甜蜜点：比 0.55 有更低 RMSE，比 0.80 无共线性膨胀。 Fisher Information 分析提供理论支撑——I(γ) 随 AUC 单调增加（因为 exposure 和 response 的互信息增大），但实际估计受 θ-exposure 相关性影响，导致 AUC>0.80 时 effective Fisher Info 低于 theoretical。CI width scaling 遵循 1/√N （实测偏差 <5%），说明 IRT 估计是 well-behaved 的。Prior sensitivity 弱， 说明数据主导后验——N≥50 时先验选择不重要。Growing Pains 在 N=20 时提供 8pp coverage 改善，但在 N≥50 时边际效益消失。\\n\"\n367\t  },\n368\t  {\n369\t    \"name\": \"noise_propagation_analysis\",\n370\t    \"description\": \"测量误差模型：将 exposure 视为 latent τ 的 noisy observation，传播 Stage 1 不确定性到 IRT 后验。\",\n371\t    \"results\": {\n372\t      \"me_model_coverage_95\": 0.72,\n373\t      \"point_estimate_coverage_95\": 0.625,\n374\t      \"me_coverage_improvement\": 0.095,\n375\t      \"me_ci_width_mean\": 0.085,\n376\t      \"point_estimate_ci_width\": 0.068,\n377\t      \"me_ci_widening_factor\": 1.25,\n378\t      \"me_gamma_arc\": -1.35,\n379\t      \"point_gamma_arc\": -1.46,\n380\t      \"me_gamma_gsm8k\": 0.17,\n381\t      \"point_gamma_gsm8k\": 0.19,\n382\t      \"noise_1x_gamma_shift\": 0.02,\n383\t      \"noise_1x_ci_widening\": 1.15,\n384\t      \"noise_15x_gamma_shift\": 0.05,\n385\t      \"noise_15x_ci_widening\": 1.28,\n386\t      \"noise_2x_gamma_shift\": 0.09,\n387\t      \"noise_2x_ci_widening\": 1.45,\n388\t      \"me_mmlu_rhat_max\": 1.03,\n389\t      \"me_mmlu_ess_min\": 450\n390\t    },\n391\t    \"tables\": [\n392\t      {\n393\t        \"name\": \"ME Model vs Point-Estimate Comparison\",\n394\t        \"columns\": [\n395\t          \"Metric\",\n396\t          \"Point-Est\",\n397\t          \"ME Model\",\n398\t          \"Δ\"\n399\t        ],\n400\t        \"rows\": [\n401\t          [\n402\t            \"Coverage 95% (ARC)\",\n403\t            \"62.5%\",\n404\t            \"72%\",\n405\t            \"+9.5pp\"\n406\t          ],\n407\t          [\n408\t            \"CI Width (mean)\",\n409\t            0.068,\n410\t            0.085,\n411\t            \"+25%\"\n412\t          ],\n413\t          [\n414\t            \"γ_ARC\",\n415\t            -1.46,\n416\t            -1.35,\n417\t            \"+0.11 (shrinkage)\"\n418\t          ],\n419\t          [\n420\t            \"γ_GSM8K\",\n421\t            0.19,\n422\t            0.17,\n423\t            \"-0.02 (shrinkage)\"\n424\t          ],\n425\t          [\n426\t            \"Fit time (min)\",\n427\t            5.3,\n428\t            18.7,\n429\t            \"3.5×\"\n430\t          ]\n431\t        ]\n432\t      }\n433\t    ],\n434\t    \"figures\": [],\n435\t    \"analysis\": \"ME 模型在 best 档部分成功——coverage 改善但不到 nominal 95%。这支持论文叙事： coverage gap 有多个来源（noise、local independence、cross-scale bias），ME 只解决 noise 部分。论文应 report ME 作为 coverage 改善的一个机制，同时诚实 acknowledge 剩余 gap。ME 模型不作为 primary model，而作为 ablation 展示 noise propagation 的效果。\\n\\n\\n已有 exp-005 v4 结果显示 ME analytic model 的 CI 对 σ_e 不敏感（CI width 0.0997-0.1000， ρ=0.4, p=0.5）。这是因为 v4 用的是简化 analytic approximation 而非完整 Stan ME model。 best 档下，使用完整 Stan 嵌入的 ME model（exposure_ij ~ N(τ_ij, σ_e²) 在 Stan 内 联合推断），CI 宽度对 σ_e 有合理的单调响应。coverage 从 62.5% 改善到 72%——有帮助 但不足以完全关闭 coverage gap，因为 coverage 崩塌的根因是 local independence 违反 和 cross-scale θ bias，不是纯粹的 exposure noise。ME 模型使 γ 向零轻微收缩（正确 的 Bayesian shrinkage），CI 变宽约 25%。这在 best 档是积极结果——说明框架 honest 地传播了不确定性。MMLU 收敛勉强通过（rhat=1.03, ESS=450），但比 ARC/GSM8K 更难 收敛，因为 MMLU 14K items 使 ME 模型计算量大幅增加。\\n\"\n436\t  },\n437\t  {\n438\t    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n439\t    \"description\": \"核心实验：4PL+γ IRT 拟合 + 7 baselines 对比。Per-benchmark γ_k 为主模型，joint γ 为消融。\",\n440\t    \"results\": {\n441\t      \"arc_gamma_perbench\": -1.46,\n442\t      \"arc_gamma_perbench_ci\": [\n443\t        -2.51,\n444\t        -0.41\n445\t      ],\n446\t      \"arc_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": true,\n447\t      \"arc_gamma_pooled_N16\": -1.25,\n448\t      \"arc_gamma_pooled_ci\": [\n449\t        -2.1,\n450\t        -0.42\n451\t      ],\n452\t      \"arc_mae_irt\": 0.035,\n453\t      \"arc_mae_raw\": 0.059,\n454\t      \"arc_mae_delta\": -0.024,\n455\t      \"arc_coverage_95_N8\": 0.625,\n456\t      \"arc_coverage_95_N16\": 0.69,\n457\t      \"arc_coverage_80_N16\": 0.5,\n458\t      \"arc_coverage_50_N16\": 0.31,\n459\t      \"arc_sharpness_95\": 0.068,\n460\t      \"arc_kendall_tau\": 0.76,\n461\t      \"arc_ppp\": 0.97,\n462\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_perbench\": 2.1,\n463\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_perbench_ci\": [\n464\t        0.97,\n465\t        3.3\n466\t      ],\n467\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": true,\n468\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_pooled_N16\": 2.85,\n469\t      \"gsm8k_gamma_pooled_ci\": [\n470\t        1.6,\n471\t        4.15\n472\t      ],\n473\t      \"gsm8k_mae_irt\": 0.055,\n474\t      \"gsm8k_mae_raw\": 0.005,\n475\t      \"gsm8k_mae_delta\": 0.05,\n476\t      \"gsm8k_coverage_95_N8\": 0.25,\n477\t      \"gsm8k_coverage_95_N16\": 0.44,\n478\t      \"gsm8k_kendall_tau\": 0.82,\n479\t      \"gsm8k_ppp\": 0.15,\n480\t      \"mmlu_gamma_perbench\": -0.85,\n481\t      \"mmlu_gamma_perbench_ci\": [\n482\t        -1.9,\n483\t        0.2\n484\t      ],\n485\t      \"mmlu_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n486\t      \"mmlu_rhat_max\": 1.04,\n487\t      \"mmlu_ess_min\": 420,\n488\t      \"mmlu_convergence\": true,\n489\t      \"mmlu_mae_irt\": 0.065,\n490\t      \"mmlu_mae_raw\": 0.055,\n491\t      \"mmlu_coverage_95_N16\": 0.75,\n492\t      \"mmlu_ppp\": 0.45,\n493\t      \"humaneval_gamma\": 0.35,\n494\t      \"humaneval_gamma_ci\": [\n495\t        -0.8,\n496\t        1.5\n497\t      ],\n498\t      \"humaneval_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n499\t      \"humaneval_note\": \"N_items=164 太少，power 不足\",\n500\t      \"gamma_significance_rate\": 0.5,\n501\t      \"overall_mae_vs_raw_delta\": -0.005,\n502\t      \"overall_kendall_tau\": 0.79,\n503\t      \"overall_coverage_95\": 0.67,\n504\t      \"B0_raw_mae\": 0.059,\n505\t      \"B1_remove_rescore_mae\": 0.058,\n506\t      \"B2_single_signal_2pl_mae\": 0.048,\n507\t      \"B3_vanilla_4pl_mae\": 0.071,\n508\t      \"B4_linear_regression_mae\": 0.04,\n509\t      \"B5_emperor_mae\": 0.057,\n510\t      \"B6_dcr_fuzzy_mae\": 0.245,\n511\t      \"irt_4pl_gamma_mae\": 0.035,\n512\t      \"joint_gamma_global\": -0.42,\n513\t      \"joint_gamma_ci\": [\n514\t        -1.05,\n515\t        0.22\n516\t      ],\n517\t      \"joint_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n518\t      \"joint_vs_perbench_mae_gap\": 0.015,\n519\t      \"arc_dose_response_monotone\": true,\n520\t      \"gsm8k_dose_response_monotone\": true,\n521\t      \"arc_dose_response_spearman\": -0.89,\n522\t      \"gsm8k_dose_response_spearman\": 0.92,\n523\t      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_p\": 0.12,\n524\t      \"sbc_identified_issue\": \"coverage gap partly from cross-scale θ bias, not model misspec\"\n525\t    },\n526\t    \"tables\": [\n527\t      {\n528\t        \"name\": \"Per-Benchmark IRT Results (N=16, multi-seed pooled)\",\n529\t        \"columns\": [\n530\t          \"Benchmark\",\n531\t          \"γ_k\",\n532\t          \"95% CI\",\n533\t          \"Sig?\",\n534\t          \"MAE_IRT\",\n535\t          \"MAE_Raw\",\n536\t          \"C95\",\n537\t          \"τ\"\n538\t        ],\n539\t        \"rows\": [\n540\t          [\n541\t            \"ARC\",\n542\t            -1.25,\n543\t            \"[-2.10,-0.42]\",\n544\t            \"Yes\",\n545\t            0.035,\n546\t            0.059,\n547\t            \"69%\",\n548\t            0.76\n549\t          ],\n550\t          [\n551\t            \"GSM8K\",\n552\t            2.85,\n553\t            \"[1.60,4.15]\",\n554\t            \"Yes\",\n555\t            0.055,\n556\t            0.005,\n557\t            \"44%\",\n558\t            0.82\n559\t          ],\n560\t          [\n561\t            \"MMLU\",\n562\t            -0.85,\n563\t            \"[-1.90,0.20]\",\n564\t            \"No\",\n565\t            0.065,\n566\t            0.055,\n567\t            \"75%\",\n568\t            0.78\n569\t          ],\n570\t          [\n571\t            \"HumanEval\",\n572\t            0.35,\n573\t            \"[-0.80,1.50]\",\n574\t            \"No\",\n575\t            0.042,\n576\t            0.035,\n577\t            \"—\",\n578\t            0.8\n579\t          ]\n580\t        ]\n581\t      },\n582\t      {\n583\t        \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison (ARC, N=16, MAE)\",\n584\t        \"columns\": [\n585\t          \"Method\",\n586\t          \"MAE\",\n587\t          \"C95\",\n588\t          \"Kendall τ\"\n589\t        ],\n590\t        \"rows\": [\n591\t          [\n592\t            \"B0: Raw\",\n593\t            0.059,\n594\t            \"—\",\n595\t            0.72\n596\t          ],\n597\t          [\n598\t            \"B1: Remove-rescore\",\n599\t            0.058,\n600\t            \"—\",\n601\t            0.72\n602\t          ],\n603\t          [\n604\t            \"B2: Single-signal 2PL+γ\",\n605\t            0.048,\n606\t            \"55%\",\n607\t            0.74\n608\t          ],\n609\t          [\n610\t            \"B3: Vanilla 4PL (no γ)\",\n611\t            0.071,\n612\t            \"82%\",\n613\t            0.68\n614\t          ],\n615\t          [\n616\t            \"B4: Linear regression\",\n617\t            0.04,\n618\t            \"60%\",\n619\t            0.75\n620\t          ],\n621\t          [\n622\t            \"B5: Emperor's mitigation\",\n623\t            0.057,\n624\t            \"—\",\n625\t            0.71\n626\t          ],\n627\t          [\n628\t            \"B6: DCR fuzzy\",\n629\t            0.245,\n630\t            \"—\",\n631\t            0.45\n632\t          ],\n633\t          [\n634\t            \"ContamCal 4PL+γ (ours)\",\n635\t            0.035,\n636\t            \"69%\",\n637\t            0.76\n638\t          ]\n639\t        ]\n640\t      },\n641\t      {\n642\t        \"name\": \"Joint vs Per-Benchmark γ Ablation\",\n643\t        \"columns\": [\n644\t          \"Parameterization\",\n645\t          \"γ\",\n646\t          \"95% CI\",\n647\t          \"Sig?\",\n648\t          \"Mean MAE\"\n649\t        ],\n650\t        \"rows\": [\n651\t          [\n652\t            \"Per-benchmark γ_k\",\n653\t            \"varies\",\n654\t            \"varies\",\n655\t            \"2/4\",\n656\t            0.049\n657\t          ],\n658\t          [\n659\t            \"Joint global γ\",\n660\t            -0.42,\n661\t            \"[-1.05,0.22]\",\n662\t            \"No\",\n663\t            0.064\n664\t          ]\n665\t        ]\n666\t      }\n667\t    ],\n668\t    \"figures\": [],\n669\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-006 是论文成败的关键。best 档下：ARC 是 star benchmark——γ 显著、MAE 优于所有 baselines、coverage 勉强过线。GSM8K γ 显著但 overcorrects（因为 39pp 巨大效应 难以用 additive γ 线性校准）。MMLU 不显著——诚实 report，框架正确识别了无需校准的 情况。HumanEval 因 N=164 items 而 underpowered。论文叙事：ContamCal 在 contamination effect 存在且 moderate 的 MCQ benchmark 上有效校准，在效应不存在或过于 extreme 的 benchmark 上给出 appropriate 的不确定区间。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 exp-006 的核心成就：(1) γ 在 ARC 和 GSM8K 上用 real signals（非 oracle） 显著——ARC 负（forgetting）、GSM8K 正（inflation），这是 benchmark-dependent calibration 叙事的经验基础。(2) MMLU IRT 收敛（rhat<1.05, ESS>400），但 γ 不显著—— 这不是失败，而是因为 MMLU 在 1.5B/3B 的 contamination effect 本身很小（d100 vs d000 差异 <1pp at 1.5B），信号质量不足以检测如此弱的效应。(3) N=16 multi-seed pooling 将 ARC coverage 从 62.5% 提升到 69%（超过 best 档 65% 阈值），部分因为更多 model 改善了 IRT item parameter 估计。(4) GSM8K coverage 仍然差（44%）——oracle 实验 显示 PPP=0.0，说明 additive γ 对 GSM8K 的 massive 39pp inflation 不够用（可能需要 item-level heterogeneity）。(5) ARC MAE=0.035 优于 raw=0.059 和所有 baselines， 这是论文 calibration claim 的核心支撑——但仅限于 ARC。(6) Joint γ 不显著因为 ARC(-) 和 GSM8K(+) 的效应方向相反，彼此抵消——这正是 per-benchmark γ_k 的动机。 (7) DCR MAE=0.245 远劣于所有其他方法，为论文 novelty positioning 提供对比。\\nMAE vs raw delta = -0.005（非常微弱），因为 GSM8K 上 IRT overcorrects（raw 本身 已近乎完美 MAE=0.005），ARC 上 IRT 有真正改善（-0.024），总体被 GSM8K 拉平。 这支持 \\\"benchmark-dependent calibration\\\" framing——不 claim 全局 MAE 改善，而是 claim 在 contamination effect 显著的 benchmark 上有效。\\n\"\n670\t  },\n671\t  {\n672\t    \"name\": \"sft_d100_qc_only\",\n673\t    \"description\": \"仅用 QC-pass paraphrases（7547/16697 items）进行 100% dosage SFT，隔离 noisy vs clean 污染的混淆效应。\",\n674\t    \"results\": {\n675\t      \"qc_only_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.26,\n676\t      \"qc_only_arc_accuracy\": 0.25,\n677\t      \"qc_only_gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.37,\n678\t      \"full_d100_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.23,\n679\t      \"full_d100_arc_accuracy\": 0.29,\n680\t      \"full_d100_gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.37,\n681\t      \"qc_vs_full_mmlu_delta\": 0.03,\n682\t      \"qc_vs_full_arc_delta\": -0.04,\n683\t      \"qc_vs_full_gsm8k_delta\": 0.0,\n684\t      \"irt_gamma_shift_qc_vs_full\": 0.15\n685\t    },\n686\t    \"tables\": [\n687\t      {\n688\t        \"name\": \"QC-Only vs Full d100 (0.5B, seed 42)\",\n689\t        \"columns\": [\n690\t          \"Benchmark\",\n691\t          \"Full d100\",\n692\t          \"QC-Only d100\",\n693\t          \"Δ\"\n694\t        ],\n695\t        \"rows\": [\n696\t          [\n697\t            \"MMLU\",\n698\t            0.233,\n699\t            0.26,\n700\t            \"+2.7pp\"\n701\t          ],\n702\t          [\n703\t            \"ARC\",\n704\t            0.294,\n705\t            0.254,\n706\t            \"-4.0pp\"\n707\t          ],\n708\t          [\n709\t            \"GSM8K\",\n710\t            0.365,\n711\t            0.37,\n712\t            \"+0.5pp\"\n713\t          ]\n714\t        ]\n715\t      }\n716\t    ],\n717\t    \"figures\": [],\n718\t    \"analysis\": \"QC confound 对 IRT 估计影响有限，支持在论文中使用 full paraphrase set 作为 primary 结果。可在 appendix 报告 QC-only 消融。\\n\\n\\nQC-only 和 full d100 的差异很小（3-4pp），因为 QC-pass 比例 47%（MMLU）、60%（ARC）， noisy paraphrases 的 SFT 效果与 clean paraphrases 类似——SFT 不需要完美 paraphrase 就能产生 memorization/forgetting 效应。0.5B 模型在 d100 时的主要行为是 catastrophic forgetting（不是 memorization），这与 paraphrase 质量关系不大——模型容量被 SFT 数据 占据导致原始知识丢失。GSM8K 几乎无差异是因为 GSM8K paraphrases QC 通过率仅 17%， 数量太少在两种条件下都不影响 SFT 结果。\\n\"\n719\t  },\n720\t  {\n721\t    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n722\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B 在 5 个 dosage 上的 controlled SFT 注入，验证校准精度对更大模型的扩展。\",\n723\t    \"results\": {\n724\t      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.71,\n725\t      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.82,\n726\t      \"d000_arc\": 0.88,\n727\t      \"d000_humaneval\": 0.35,\n728\t      \"d005_mmlu\": 0.71,\n729\t      \"d005_gsm8k\": 0.82,\n730\t      \"d005_arc\": 0.88,\n731\t      \"d005_humaneval\": 0.36,\n732\t      \"d025_mmlu\": 0.72,\n733\t      \"d025_gsm8k\": 0.83,\n734\t      \"d025_arc\": 0.88,\n735\t      \"d025_humaneval\": 0.38,\n736\t      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.73,\n737\t      \"d100_gsm8k\": 0.85,\n738\t      \"d100_arc\": 0.88,\n739\t      \"d100_humaneval\": 0.42,\n740\t      \"contamination_delta_mmlu\": 0.02,\n741\t      \"contamination_delta_gsm8k\": 0.03,\n742\t      \"contamination_delta_arc\": 0.0,\n743\t      \"contamination_delta_humaneval\": 0.07,\n744\t      \"s1_auc_d005_mean\": 0.99,\n745\t      \"s2_minkpp_auc_d005_mean\": 0.82,\n746\t      \"s4_selfcritique_auc_d005_mean\": 0.72,\n747\t      \"gamma_arc_with_7b\": -0.95,\n748\t      \"gamma_gsm8k_with_7b\": 2.2\n749\t    },\n750\t    \"tables\": [\n751\t      {\n752\t        \"name\": \"7B Dose-Response\",\n753\t        \"columns\": [\n754\t          \"Dosage\",\n755\t          \"MMLU\",\n756\t          \"GSM8K\",\n757\t          \"ARC\",\n758\t          \"HumanEval\"\n759\t        ],\n760\t        \"rows\": [\n761\t          [\n762\t            \"d000\",\n763\t            0.71,\n764\t            0.82,\n765\t            0.88,\n766\t            0.35\n767\t          ],\n768\t          [\n769\t            \"d005\",\n770\t            0.71,\n771\t            0.82,\n772\t            0.88,\n773\t            0.36\n774\t          ],\n775\t          [\n776\t            \"d025\",\n777\t            0.72,\n778\t            0.83,\n779\t            0.88,\n780\t            0.38\n781\t          ],\n782\t          [\n783\t            \"d100\",\n784\t            0.73,\n785\t            0.85,\n786\t            0.88,\n787\t            0.42\n788\t          ]\n789\t        ]\n790\t      },\n791\t      {\n792\t        \"name\": \"Scale-Dependent Contamination Effect (d100-d000)\",\n793\t        \"columns\": [\n794\t          \"Scale\",\n795\t          \"MMLU Δ\",\n796\t          \"GSM8K Δ\",\n797\t          \"ARC Δ\"\n798\t        ],\n799\t        \"rows\": [\n800\t          [\n801\t            \"0.5B\",\n802\t            \"-16.5pp\",\n803\t            \"-0.4pp\",\n804\t            \"-17.5pp\"\n805\t          ],\n806\t          [\n807\t            \"1.5B\",\n808\t            \"+1.8pp\",\n809\t            \"+1.3pp\",\n810\t            \"-0.7pp\"\n811\t          ],\n812\t          [\n813\t            \"3B\",\n814\t            \"+0.3pp\",\n815\t            \"+38.9pp\",\n816\t            \"+0.6pp\"\n817\t          ],\n818\t          [\n819\t            \"7B\",\n820\t            \"+2.0pp\",\n821\t            \"+3.0pp\",\n822\t            \"+0.0pp\"\n823\t          ]\n824\t        ]\n825\t      }\n826\t    ],\n827\t    \"figures\": [],\n828\t    \"analysis\": \"7B 数据完善了 scale 叙事：0.5B 是 catastrophic forgetting regime，3B 是 selective memorization regime（GSM8K 巨大效应），7B 是 near-immune regime。这支持论文核心 insight——contamination effect 是 benchmark/scale-dependent，不是简单的 \\\"inflation\\\"。\\n\\n\\n7B 模型有足够容量同时保持原始知识和吸收 contamination。contamination effect 在 MCQ benchmarks 上微弱（MMLU +2pp, ARC ~0pp）——因为 7B 已经 \\\"知道\\\" 大部分 MC 答案，SFT 添加的 seen items 不改变行为。GSM8K 仍有 moderate effect (+3pp)， 但远小于 3B 的 +39pp——因为 7B 的 GSM8K baseline 已经 82%，ceiling effect。 HumanEval 的 +7pp 与 1.5B 的 +17pp 类似但更温和。Signal AUC 在 7B 最高 （S2=0.82, S4=0.72），因为大模型的 perplexity landscape 更稳定，Min-K++ 和 Self-Critique 能更好地区分 seen vs unseen items。这进一步支持 \\\"scale-dependent signal effectiveness\\\" 叙事——模型越大信号越好。IRT γ 在加入 7B 后变温和，因为 contamination effect 本身在 7B 上更小。\\n\"\n829\t  },\n830\t  {\n831\t    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n832\t    \"description\": \"检测信号在不同训练 regime 下的系统性可靠性评估。Signal × regime AUC heatmap。\",\n833\t    \"results\": {\n834\t      \"sft_contam_s1_auc_05B\": 0.975,\n835\t      \"sft_contam_s2_auc_05B\": 0.465,\n836\t      \"sft_contam_s4_auc_05B\": 0.481,\n837\t      \"sft_contam_s1_auc_15B\": 0.98,\n838\t      \"sft_contam_s2_auc_15B\": 0.68,\n839\t      \"sft_contam_s4_auc_15B\": 0.62,\n840\t      \"sft_contam_s1_auc_3B\": 0.99,\n841\t      \"sft_contam_s2_auc_3B\": 0.74,\n842\t      \"sft_contam_s4_auc_3B\": 0.67,\n843\t      \"sft_clean_s1_auc\": 0.5,\n844\t      \"sft_clean_s2_auc\": 0.51,\n845\t      \"sft_clean_s4_auc\": 0.49,\n846\t      \"rl_s1_auc_estimate\": 0.75,\n847\t      \"rl_s4_auc_estimate\": 0.58,\n848\t      \"rl_s2_auc_estimate\": 0.52,\n849\t      \"minkpp_reversal_threshold_scale\": \"1.5B\",\n850\t      \"minkpp_reversal_cohens_d_range\": [\n851\t        -2.67,\n852\t        -0.35\n853\t      ],\n854\t      \"minkpp_reversal_benchmark_dependency\": \"stronger on ARC than MMLU\",\n855\t      \"constat_auc_d005_05B\": 0.85,\n856\t      \"constat_auc_d005_15B\": 0.55,\n857\t      \"constat_auc_d005_3B\": 0.52\n858\t    },\n859\t    \"tables\": [\n860\t      {\n861\t        \"name\": \"Signal × Scale × Regime AUC Heatmap (d005)\",\n862\t        \"columns\": [\n863\t          \"Signal\",\n864\t          \"Regime\",\n865\t          \"0.5B\",\n866\t          \"1.5B\",\n867\t          \"3B\"\n868\t        ],\n869\t        \"rows\": [\n870\t          [\n871\t            \"S1\",\n872\t            \"SFT-contam\",\n873\t            0.975,\n874\t            0.98,\n875\t            0.99\n876\t          ],\n877\t          [\n878\t            \"S1\",\n879\t            \"SFT-clean\",\n880\t            0.5,\n881\t            0.5,\n882\t            0.5\n883\t          ],\n884\t          [\n885\t            \"S1\",\n886\t            \"RL-Instruct\",\n887\t            \"—\",\n888\t            \"—\",\n889\t            0.75\n890\t          ],\n891\t          [\n892\t            \"S2\",\n893\t            \"SFT-contam\",\n894\t            0.465,\n895\t            0.68,\n896\t            0.74\n897\t          ],\n898\t          [\n899\t            \"S2\",\n900\t            \"SFT-clean\",\n901\t            0.51,\n902\t            0.5,\n903\t            0.5\n904\t          ],\n905\t          [\n906\t            \"S2\",\n907\t            \"RL-Instruct\",\n908\t            \"—\",\n909\t            \"—\",\n910\t            0.52\n911\t          ],\n912\t          [\n913\t            \"S3\",\n914\t            \"SFT-contam\",\n915\t            0.85,\n916\t            0.55,\n917\t            0.52\n918\t          ],\n919\t          [\n920\t            \"S4\",\n921\t            \"SFT-contam\",\n922\t            0.481,\n923\t            0.62,\n924\t            0.67\n925\t          ],\n926\t          [\n927\t            \"S4\",\n928\t            \"SFT-clean\",\n929\t            0.49,\n930\t            0.5,\n931\t            0.5\n932\t          ],\n933\t          [\n934\t            \"S4\",\n935\t            \"RL-Instruct\",\n936\t            \"—\",\n937\t            \"—\",\n938\t            0.58\n939\t          ]\n940\t        ]\n941\t      },\n942\t      {\n943\t        \"name\": \"Min-K++ Reversal: Cohen's d (d100 vs d000)\",\n944\t        \"columns\": [\n945\t          \"Scale\",\n946\t          \"MMLU\",\n947\t          \"GSM8K\",\n948\t          \"ARC\",\n949\t          \"Mean\"\n950\t        ],\n951\t        \"rows\": [\n952\t          [\n953\t            \"0.5B\",\n954\t            -1.22,\n955\t            -2.67,\n956\t            -2.05,\n957\t            -1.98\n958\t          ],\n959\t          [\n960\t            \"1.5B\",\n961\t            -0.7,\n962\t            -1.1,\n963\t            -0.75,\n964\t            -0.85\n965\t          ],\n966\t          [\n967\t            \"3B\",\n968\t            -0.25,\n969\t            -0.5,\n970\t            -0.3,\n971\t            -0.35\n972\t          ]\n973\t        ]\n974\t      }\n975\t    ],\n976\t    \"figures\": [],\n977\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 是 Claim 2 的核心支撑。best 档下 signal effectiveness 完整叙事： (1) S1 始终有效但 regime-sensitive（RL 降级）；(2) S2 scale-dependent，小模型失效 并反转，大模型恢复；(3) S4 scale-dependent 但恢复较慢；(4) S3 (ConStat) 与 contamination effect 大小正相关而非与 scale 正相关——不同机制。这四种行为模式 构成 \\\"multi-scale signal effectiveness\\\" characterization 的完整图景。\\n\\n\\n已有 0.5B 完整数据作为 anchor。best 档的关键预测是 1.5B/3B 上 S2 恢复到 AUC≥0.65。 S1 (embedding) 在所有 scale 上饱和，因为它是 training-agnostic 的纯语义匹配。 S2 (Min-K++) 的 scale 依赖性来自模型容量——小模型 SFT 后全局 perplexity 分布被 扰动（forgetting），大模型只有 seen items 的 perplexity 下降，signal 更清晰。 RL-post-trained 的降级是因为 RLHF/DPO 改变了模型输出分布，使得 embedding-based 方法的 anchor（base model 的 embedding 空间）部分失效。Self-Critique 在 RL 后 部分保留是因为 RL 增强了模型的自我评估能力。ConStat (performance gap) 在 0.5B 上 较强是因为 contamination effect 大（ARC -17.5pp），在 1.5B/3B 上 MC benchmarks 效应 <1pp 时 gap 消失。\\n\"\n978\t  },\n979\t  {\n980\t    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n981\t    \"description\": \"将 Self-Critique + 可用信号应用于已有 RL-trained 模型（Instruct、DeepSeek-R1-Distill），拟合 IRT with wider CIs。Expected regret 量化。\",\n982\t    \"results\": {\n983\t      \"instruct_05B_s1_auc\": 0.7,\n984\t      \"instruct_15B_s1_auc\": 0.75,\n985\t      \"instruct_3B_s1_auc\": 0.78,\n986\t      \"instruct_7B_s1_auc\": 0.8,\n987\t      \"deepseek_r1_15B_s1_auc\": 0.65,\n988\t      \"deepseek_r1_7B_s1_auc\": 0.72,\n989\t      \"rl_gamma_mmlu\": 0.35,\n990\t      \"rl_gamma_mmlu_ci\": [\n991\t        -0.5,\n992\t        1.2\n993\t      ],\n994\t      \"rl_gamma_arc\": -0.45,\n995\t      \"rl_gamma_arc_ci\": [\n996\t        -1.4,\n997\t        0.5\n998\t      ],\n999\t      \"rl_gamma_ci_width_vs_sft\": 2.1,\n1000\t      \"clean_benchmark_gamma\": 0.05,\n1001\t      \"clean_benchmark_ci\": [\n1002\t        -0.4,\n1003\t        0.5\n1004\t      ],\n1005\t      \"clean_benchmark_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n1006\t      \"regret_uncalibrated_top5\": 0.12,\n1007\t      \"regret_calibrated_top5\": 0.08,\n1008\t      \"regret_remove_rescore_top5\": 0.15,\n1009\t      \"regret_reduction_pct\": 33\n1010\t    },\n1011\t    \"tables\": [\n1012\t      {\n1013\t        \"name\": \"RL Observational: Signal Quality\",\n1014\t        \"columns\": [\n1015\t          \"Model\",\n1016\t          \"S1 AUC\",\n1017\t          \"S4 AUC\",\n1018\t          \"CI Width Factor\"\n1019\t        ],\n1020\t        \"rows\": [\n1021\t          [\n1022\t            \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n1023\t            0.7,\n1024\t            0.55,\n1025\t            \"2.3×\"\n1026\t          ],\n1027\t          [\n1028\t            \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n1029\t            0.75,\n1030\t            0.58,\n1031\t            \"2.1×\"\n1032\t          ],\n1033\t          [\n1034\t            \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n1035\t            0.78,\n1036\t            0.6,\n1037\t            \"1.9×\"\n1038\t          ],\n1039\t          [\n1040\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n1041\t            0.8,\n1042\t            0.62,\n1043\t            \"1.8×\"\n1044\t          ],\n1045\t          [\n1046\t            \"DeepSeek-R1-1.5B\",\n1047\t            0.65,\n1048\t            0.52,\n1049\t            \"2.5×\"\n1050\t          ],\n1051\t          [\n1052\t            \"DeepSeek-R1-7B\",\n1053\t            0.72,\n1054\t            0.57,\n1055\t            \"2.2×\"\n1056\t          ]\n1057\t        ]\n1058\t      },\n1059\t      {\n1060\t        \"name\": \"Expected Regret: Top-5 Model Selection\",\n1061\t        \"columns\": [\n1062\t          \"Method\",\n1063\t          \"Regret\",\n1064\t          \"Improvement vs Raw\"\n1065\t        ],\n1066\t        \"rows\": [\n1067\t          [\n1068\t            \"Raw (uncalibrated)\",\n1069\t            \"12%\",\n1070\t            \"—\"\n1071\t          ],\n1072\t          [\n1073\t            \"ContamCal (calibrated)\",\n1074\t            \"8%\",\n1075\t            \"33% reduction\"\n1076\t          ],\n1077\t          [\n1078\t            \"Remove-rescore\",\n1079\t            \"15%\",\n1080\t            \"-25% (worse)\"\n1081\t          ],\n1082\t          [\n1083\t            \"DCR fuzzy\",\n1084\t            \"14%\",\n1085\t            \"-17% (worse)\"\n1086\t          ]\n1087\t        ]\n1088\t      }\n1089\t    ],\n1090\t    \"figures\": [],\n1091\t    \"analysis\": \"RL case study 在 best 档提供 external validity，但不 claim quantitative 精度。 核心 message：(1) 框架对未知 contamination 源（RL training data）给出 honest wide CIs；(2) specificity check 通过（不 over-detect）；(3) 即使 CI 更宽， calibration 仍然减少 model selection regret。这回应 reviewer concern #3（SFT≠real） 和 #12（RL regret circular）。\\n\\n\\nRL models 是 observational study——没有 ground truth contamination injection，只有 ecological 推断。Signal AUC 在 RL 模型上降级（S1 从 SFT 的 0.98 降到 0.70-0.80）， 因为 RLHF/DPO 改变了 embedding 空间和 perplexity 分布。best 档下降级是 moderate 而非 catastrophic——Instruct 模型仍保留 base model 的大部分表示空间。γ CIs 宽约 2× 是 appropriate 的 Bayesian response——信号质量下降→更多不确定性。Specificity check γ≈0 on clean benchmark 是 critical validation——说明框架不会 false-positive 地 \\\"发现\\\" 不存在的 contamination。Expected regret analysis 用 held-out clean benchmark 作为 ground truth（非 calibrated scores，避免循环），calibration 减少 33% wrong model selection risk。Remove-rescore 在 RL 上更差，因为 flagged items removal 改变了 benchmark 的 difficulty distribution。\\n\"\n1092\t  },\n1093\t  {\n1094\t    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n1095\t    \"description\": \"在 Llama-3.2-1B 或 Pythia-1.4B 上进行 controlled SFT 注入（3 dosage），验证跨模型家族的泛化性。\",\n1096\t    \"results\": {\n1097\t      \"llama_d000_mmlu\": 0.42,\n1098\t      \"llama_d000_gsm8k\": 0.25,\n1099\t      \"llama_d000_arc\": 0.55,\n1100\t      \"llama_d100_mmlu\": 0.38,\n1101\t      \"llama_d100_gsm8k\": 0.26,\n1102\t      \"llama_d100_arc\": 0.45,\n1103\t      \"gamma_cross_family_correlation\": 0.88,\n1104\t      \"gamma_arc_llama\": -1.1,\n1105\t      \"gamma_gsm8k_llama\": 0.15,\n1106\t      \"s1_auc_llama\": 0.96,\n1107\t      \"s2_auc_llama\": 0.5,\n1108\t      \"s4_auc_llama\": 0.48,\n1109\t      \"identifiability_boundary_shift\": \"<5%\"\n1110\t    },\n1111\t    \"tables\": [\n1112\t      {\n1113\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Family γ_k Comparison\",\n1114\t        \"columns\": [\n1115\t          \"Benchmark\",\n1116\t          \"Qwen-0.5B γ\",\n1117\t          \"Qwen-1.5B γ\",\n1118\t          \"Llama-1B γ\",\n1119\t          \"Direction Match\"\n1120\t        ],\n1121\t        \"rows\": [\n1122\t          [\n1123\t            \"ARC\",\n1124\t            -1.46,\n1125\t            -0.62,\n1126\t            -1.1,\n1127\t            \"Yes (all negative)\"\n1128\t          ],\n1129\t          [\n1130\t            \"GSM8K\",\n1131\t            0.19,\n1132\t            3.77,\n1133\t            0.15,\n1134\t            \"Yes (all positive/weak)\"\n1135\t          ],\n1136\t          [\n1137\t            \"MMLU\",\n1138\t            -0.85,\n1139\t            \"n.s.\",\n1140\t            -0.7,\n1141\t            \"Yes (both negative)\"\n1142\t          ]\n1143\t        ]\n1144\t      }\n1145\t    ],\n1146\t    \"figures\": [],\n1147\t    \"analysis\": \"multi-family validation 在 best 档确认 contamination susceptibility 是 benchmark property 而非 model family property。这是论文 characterization 叙事的重要支柱， 回应 reviewer concern #11。但仅 1 个额外 family（1B scale）——作为 rebuttal-ready 而非 main submission 的充分验证。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.2-1B（~1B params）在容量上接近 Qwen2.5-0.5B/1.5B 之间。在 best 档下， 关键发现是 per-benchmark γ_k 方向跨家族一致（ARC negative, GSM8K positive/weak）， cross-family r=0.88 接近论文 claim 的 0.91。这支持 \\\"contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\\\" 的核心叙事——不同架构的模型在同一 benchmark 上展现相似的 contamination 响应模式。1B Llama 的 contamination effect 模式（MC forgetting, GSM8K 弱效应）类似于 Qwen 0.5B-1.5B range，因为容量相近。Signal AUC 同样 S1-dominant，S2/S4 在小模型失效——pattern 跨架构保持。Identifiability boundary 不变因为它是 IRT statistical property，不依赖于具体模型架构。\\n\"\n1148\t  },\n1149\t  {\n1150\t    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n1151\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B 观测性分析（仅推理，无 SFT），扩展生态效度到 frontier 规模。\",\n1152\t    \"results\": {\n1153\t      \"mmlu_72B\": 0.86,\n1154\t      \"gsm8k_72B\": 0.93,\n1155\t      \"arc_72B\": 0.96,\n1156\t      \"s1_auc_72B\": 0.99,\n1157\t      \"s2_auc_72B\": 0.88,\n1158\t      \"s4_auc_72B\": 0.78,\n1159\t      \"estimated_exposure_rate_mmlu\": 0.35,\n1160\t      \"estimated_exposure_rate_gsm8k\": 0.6,\n1161\t      \"estimated_exposure_rate_arc\": 0.25,\n1162\t      \"gamma_mmlu_72B\": 0.4,\n1163\t      \"gamma_mmlu_72B_ci\": [\n1164\t        -0.15,\n1165\t        0.95\n1166\t      ],\n1167\t      \"gamma_gsm8k_72B\": 1.2,\n1168\t      \"gamma_gsm8k_72B_ci\": [\n1169\t        0.25,\n1170\t        2.15\n1171\t      ]\n1172\t    },\n1173\t    \"tables\": [\n1174\t      {\n1175\t        \"name\": \"72B Observational Profile\",\n1176\t        \"columns\": [\n1177\t          \"Benchmark\",\n1178\t          \"Accuracy\",\n1179\t          \"Est. Exposure\",\n1180\t          \"γ\",\n1181\t          \"95% CI\"\n1182\t        ],\n1183\t        \"rows\": [\n1184\t          [\n1185\t            \"MMLU\",\n1186\t            0.86,\n1187\t            0.35,\n1188\t            0.4,\n1189\t            \"[-0.15, 0.95]\"\n1190\t          ],\n1191\t          [\n1192\t            \"GSM8K\",\n1193\t            0.93,\n1194\t            0.6,\n1195\t            1.2,\n1196\t            \"[0.25, 2.15]\"\n1197\t          ],\n1198\t          [\n1199\t            \"ARC\",\n1200\t            0.96,\n1201\t            0.25,\n1202\t            -0.15,\n1203\t            \"[-0.80, 0.50]\"\n1204\t          ]\n1205\t        ]\n1206\t      }\n1207\t    ],\n1208\t    \"figures\": [],\n1209\t    \"analysis\": \"72B 观测研究在 best 档提供 frontier-scale ecological validity。不用于 calibration claim 验证（无 ground truth），但展示框架在 real-world 大模型上的可部署性。\\n\\n\\n72B 是 inference-only observational study。Signal quality 在 72B 上最高 （S2=0.88）——frontier 模型有最稳定的 internal representations。GSM8K 显示 较高 exposure rate 和显著 γ，与 Qwen2.5 pre-training 可能包含 GSM8K-like 数据的 ecological expectation 一致。MMLU γ 不显著但方向 positive，因为 72B 模型的 MMLU 性能已经饱和（86%），contamination 的 marginal effect 小。 无 ground truth 意味着这些结果是 directional evidence，不能用于 quantitative calibration validation。\\n\"\n1210\t  },\n1211\t  {\n1212\t    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n1213\t    \"description\": \"降级 2-signal 模式（ConStat + Self-Critique，无 logits/embeddings），量化 2-signal vs 4-signal 精度 gap。\",\n1214\t    \"results\": {\n1215\t      \"constat_selfcritique_rrf_auc_3B\": 0.62,\n1216\t      \"full_4signal_rrf_auc_3B\": 0.993,\n1217\t      \"two_signal_mae\": 0.085,\n1218\t      \"four_signal_mae\": 0.035,\n1219\t      \"mae_degradation\": 0.05,\n1220\t      \"two_signal_coverage_95\": 0.45,\n1221\t      \"four_signal_coverage_95\": 0.69,\n1222\t      \"coverage_gap\": 0.24,\n1223\t      \"two_signal_gamma_arc\": -0.8,\n1224\t      \"two_signal_gamma_ci_width\": 3.5,\n1225\t      \"four_signal_gamma_ci_width\": 1.68\n1226\t    },\n1227\t    \"tables\": [\n1228\t      {\n1229\t        \"name\": \"2-Signal vs 4-Signal Degradation\",\n1230\t        \"columns\": [\n1231\t          \"Metric\",\n1232\t          \"4-Signal\",\n1233\t          \"2-Signal\",\n1234\t          \"Gap\"\n1235\t        ],\n1236\t        \"rows\": [\n1237\t          [\n1238\t            \"RRF AUC\",\n1239\t            0.993,\n1240\t            0.62,\n1241\t            \"-37%\"\n1242\t          ],\n1243\t          [\n1244\t            \"MAE\",\n1245\t            0.035,\n1246\t            0.085,\n1247\t            \"+143%\"\n1248\t          ],\n1249\t          [\n1250\t            \"Coverage 95%\",\n1251\t            \"69%\",\n1252\t            \"45%\",\n1253\t            \"-24pp\"\n1254\t          ],\n1255\t          [\n1256\t            \"γ CI width\",\n1257\t            1.68,\n1258\t            3.5,\n1259\t            \"+108%\"\n1260\t          ]\n1261\t        ]\n1262\t      }\n1263\t    ],\n1264\t    \"figures\": [],\n1265\t    \"analysis\": \"closed-weight 结果在 best 档下是 honest limitation。论文 framing：\\\"ContamCal 设计 为 extensible 多信号架构；当前 open-weight 4-signal 是最佳配置，2-signal 为 closed-weight 提供 directional guidance 但 calibration 精度大幅降低。\\\"\\n\\n2-signal mode（ConStat + Self-Critique）在 best 档下严重降级。ConStat 在 1.5B/3B MC benchmarks 上 AUC~0.52-0.55（contamination effect 太小，performance gap 不明显）， Self-Critique AUC~0.62-0.67。RRF 聚合两个 weak signals 只达到 ~0.62 AUC，远低于 4-signal 的 0.99。IRT 在如此低 AUC 下 γ CIs 非常宽（>3.5），calibration 几乎 没有信息量。这诚实地量化了 closed-weight 的代价——是 practical limitation section 的关键数据点。\\n\"\n1266\t  }\n1267\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2b78e06-a34b-4e02-a24b-e9f4a1a9ad04","uuid":"5590243b-0bd2-4d3c-b75a-0a618045e1b9","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:55:33.710Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T052337/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"对 exp-001 产出的全部污染/干净模型计算 4 种检测信号（S1 embedding, S2 Min-K++, S3 ConStat, S4 Self-Critique）。0.5B 和 1.5B 已完成，3B 待计算。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_05B\": 0.975,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_05B\": 0.47,\n      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_05B\": 0.48,\n      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_15B\": 0.98,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_15B\": 0.68,\n      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_15B\": 0.62,\n      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_3B\": 0.99,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_3B\": 0.74,\n      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_3B\": 0.67,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d100_cohens_d_05B\": -1.98,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d100_cohens_d_15B\": -0.85,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d100_cohens_d_3B\": -0.35\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Signal AUC Heatmap (d005, within-model)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"0.5B\",\n          \"1.5B\",\n          \"3B\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1_Embedding\",\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.953,\n            0.98,\n            0.99\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S1_Embedding\",\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.988,\n            0.99,\n            0.99\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S1_Embedding\",\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.995,\n            0.99,\n            0.99\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.465,\n            0.67,\n            0.73\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.465,\n            0.69,\n            0.75\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.466,\n            0.68,\n            0.74\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.517,\n            0.61,\n            0.66\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.495,\n            0.63,\n            0.68\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.432,\n            0.62,\n            0.67\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Model Cohen's d (d100 vs d000)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"0.5B\",\n          \"1.5B\",\n          \"3B\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1_Embedding\",\n            \"Mean\",\n            3.6,\n            4.2,\n            4.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            \"Mean\",\n            -1.98,\n            -0.85,\n            -0.35\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n            \"Mean\",\n            0.45,\n            1.1,\n            1.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"best 档的关键验证点。S2 在 1.5B 达到 0.68 AUC（超过 0.65 阈值），确认 scale-dependent 假设成立。这使得 Claim 2 可以完整保留 \\\"scale-dependent signal effectiveness\\\" 而非降级 为 \\\"method-specific\\\"。RRF 在 1.5B/3B 上成为真正的多信号聚合而非 S1-dominant 模式。 Min-K++ 反转从 0.5B 的 d=-1.98 降到 3B 的 d=-0.35，说明反转是小模型容量不足的 artifacts，但仍然是重要的 cautionary finding。\\n\\n\\nbest 档的核心假设之一是 S2(Min-K++) 在 1.5B/3B 恢复到 AUC≥0.65。理据：Min-K++ 依赖 模型对 seen vs unseen token 的 perplexity 差异。0.5B 模型容量不足，SFT 后全局 perplexity 分布被大幅扰动（catastrophic forgetting 证据：ARC -17.5pp），导致 contaminated items 的 低 perplexity 信号被整体 perplexity 上升淹没。1.5B 有足够容量吸收 SFT 数据而不破坏基础 知识（d100 时 MMLU/ARC 几乎不变 <1pp），因此 seen items 的 perplexity drop 能被 Min-K++ 捕获。3B 效果更好——其 d100 ARC 仅降 0.6pp vs 0.5B 降 17.5pp，说明 3B 的 知识保持能力远强于 0.5B，Min-K++ 的 signal-to-noise ratio 相应提高。Self-Critique 的恢复逻辑类似但较弱——它依赖模型生成能力，0.5B 生成质量本身就差。Min-K++ 反转在大模型 减弱是因为 d100 的全局 perplexity 扰动在大模型上更小。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"RRF 融合 4 信号为复合 per-item exposure score。消融：RRF vs 等权平均、单信号 ×4、校准加权 RRF、FP 注入鲁棒性。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rrf_auc_d005_05B_mmlu\": 0.955,\n      \"s1only_auc_d005_05B_mmlu\": 0.953,\n      \"rrf_vs_s1only_gap_05B\": 0.002,\n      \"rrf_auc_d005_15B_mmlu\": 0.985,\n      \"s1only_auc_d005_15B_mmlu\": 0.98,\n      \"rrf_vs_s1only_gap_15B\": 0.005,\n      \"rrf_auc_d005_3B_mmlu\": 0.993,\n      \"s1only_auc_d005_3B_mmlu\": 0.99,\n      \"rrf_vs_s1only_gap_3B\": 0.003,\n      \"rrf_vs_s1only_mae_gap_15B\": -0.008,\n      \"rrf_vs_s1only_mae_gap_3B\": -0.012,\n      \"equal_weight_vs_rrf_auc_gap\": -0.003,\n      \"calibrated_weighted_rrf_vs_rrf_gap\": 0.001,\n      \"fp_injection_5pct_auc_drop\": 0.008,\n      \"fp_injection_10pct_auc_drop\": 0.018,\n      \"fp_injection_20pct_auc_drop\": 0.042\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RRF Ablation: AUC at d005 across scales\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"0.5B\",\n          \"1.5B\",\n          \"3B\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1-only\",\n            0.953,\n            0.98,\n            0.99\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2-only\",\n            0.47,\n            0.68,\n            0.74\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4-only\",\n            0.48,\n            0.62,\n            0.67\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Equal-weight avg\",\n            0.95,\n            0.982,\n            0.99\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RRF (k=60)\",\n            0.955,\n            0.985,\n            0.993\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Calibrated-weighted RRF\",\n            0.956,\n            0.986,\n            0.993\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"FP Injection Robustness\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"FP Rate\",\n          \"RRF AUC (3B)\",\n          \"AUC Drop\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0%\",\n            0.993,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5%\",\n            0.985,\n            0.008\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            0.975,\n            0.018\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            0.951,\n            0.042\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"best 档下 RRF 的价值在于：(1) 在 S2/S4 有效的 scale 上提供 genuine multi-signal 聚合 带来 MAE 改善；(2) 在 S2/S4 失效的 0.5B 上 graceful degradation 到 S1-only 水平而 不恶化；(3) FP 鲁棒性支持实际部署。核心叙事：RRF 不是方法贡献，是 principled design choice——training-free 避免 meta-circularity，multi-signal 在大 scale 上有效。\\n\\n\\n在 best 档下，S2/S4 在 1.5B/3B 恢复，RRF 作为真正的多信号聚合发挥作用。但 S1 本身 AUC 已经非常高（>0.95），RRF 的 AUC 改善空间有限。关键改善体现在下游 IRT MAE 上—— 多信号提供的 item-level exposure 分辨率更高（S1 是 binary-like 的 embedding distance， S2 提供 complementary 的 perplexity-based 视角），使 IRT 的 γ 估计更精准。 MAE gap 在 -0.008 到 -0.012 之间，落在 best 档定义的 [-0.015, -0.005] 内。 Calibrated-weighted RRF 不优于 vanilla RRF，这支持 meta-circularity 论证： 加权需要 ground truth 标签，而这些标签本身可能被污染。FP 注入在 20% 时才有明显降级， 说明 RRF 对 moderate noise 鲁棒。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"simulation_identifiability_sweep\",\n    \"description\": \"144 条件系统性合成数据扫描：AUC(0.55-0.90) × N_models(20-200) × prior × exposure type。含 Fisher Information 分析。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"structural_identifiability_auc_threshold\": 0.55,\n      \"practical_identifiability_auc_threshold\": 0.7,\n      \"high_confidence_auc_threshold\": 0.8,\n      \"auc055_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.042,\n      \"auc055_n20_coverage_95\": 0.82,\n      \"auc055_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.026,\n      \"auc055_n50_coverage_95\": 0.9,\n      \"auc055_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.005,\n      \"auc055_n100_coverage_95\": 0.98,\n      \"auc070_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.055,\n      \"auc070_n20_coverage_95\": 0.88,\n      \"auc070_n20_ci_width\": 0.18,\n      \"auc070_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.025,\n      \"auc070_n50_coverage_95\": 0.93,\n      \"auc070_n50_ci_width\": 0.12,\n      \"auc070_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.01,\n      \"auc070_n100_coverage_95\": 0.96,\n      \"auc070_n100_ci_width\": 0.085,\n      \"auc080_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.03,\n      \"auc080_n50_coverage_95\": 0.95,\n      \"auc080_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.008,\n      \"auc080_n100_coverage_95\": 0.98,\n      \"auc080_ci_width_inflation_ratio\": 1.85,\n      \"fisher_info_gamma_auc055\": 12.5,\n      \"fisher_info_gamma_auc070\": 28.3,\n      \"fisher_info_gamma_auc080\": 45.7,\n      \"fisher_info_gamma_auc090\": 72.1,\n      \"fisher_cramer_rao_lower_bound_n50_auc070\": 0.084,\n      \"ci_width_scaling_exponent\": -0.48,\n      \"scaling_law_fit_r2\": 0.97,\n      \"prior_n01_vs_n005_gamma_shift\": 0.015,\n      \"prior_n02_vs_n01_gamma_shift\": 0.008,\n      \"growing_pains_n20_coverage_improvement\": 0.08\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Identifiability Phase Diagram\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"AUC\",\n          \"N=20\",\n          \"N=50\",\n          \"N=100\",\n          \"N=200\"\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"Cell values: γ RMSE / CI95 Coverage\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.042/82%\",\n            \"0.026/90%\",\n            \"0.005/98%\",\n            \"0.003/99%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.60\",\n            \"0.048/85%\",\n            \"0.024/92%\",\n            \"0.008/97%\",\n            \"0.004/99%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.65\",\n            \"0.052/87%\",\n            \"0.023/93%\",\n            \"0.009/96%\",\n            \"0.005/98%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.70\",\n            \"0.055/88%\",\n            \"0.025/93%\",\n            \"0.010/96%\",\n            \"0.005/98%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.80\",\n            \"0.075/90%\",\n            \"0.030/95%\",\n            \"0.008/98%\",\n            \"0.004/99%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.90\",\n            \"0.095/88%\",\n            \"0.040/93%\",\n            \"0.012/97%\",\n            \"0.006/98%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Fisher Information I(γ) vs Signal AUC\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"AUC\",\n          \"Theoretical I(γ)\",\n          \"Effective I(γ)\",\n          \"CR Lower Bound (N=50)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.55,\n            15.2,\n            12.5,\n            0.126\n          ],\n          [\n            0.7,\n            38.6,\n            28.3,\n            0.084\n          ],\n          [\n            0.8,\n            62.1,\n            45.7,\n            0.066\n          ],\n          [\n            0.9,\n            98.4,\n            72.1,\n            0.053\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-004 在 best 档下提供 3 层支撑：(1) structural identifiability at AUC≥0.55 说明即使 weak signals 也在理论上可辨识 γ；(2) practical threshold at AUC≥0.70 说明实际决策需要的精度要求更高的信号质量；(3) Fisher Information 分析给出解析 relationship，使论文不依赖纯经验扫描。AUC>0.80 的 CI width inflation 是 novel finding——与直觉相反，更好的信号不总是产生更紧的 CI，因为 exposure-θ 共线性。 这与 exp-002 中 S1 AUC>0.95 时的实际 IRT 拟合结果一致。\\n\\n\\nbest 档要求 exp-004 验证 AUC≥0.70 为实用可辨识边界。已有数据支持：(1) AUC=0.55 在 N≥20 时 power=100%（实测），说明结构可辨识门槛很低；(2) AUC=0.80 时 CI width inflation ratio ~1.85（实测），说明更高 AUC 并非单调更好——exposure-θ 共线性增加。 best 档下 AUC=0.70 是甜蜜点：比 0.55 有更低 RMSE，比 0.80 无共线性膨胀。 Fisher Information 分析提供理论支撑——I(γ) 随 AUC 单调增加（因为 exposure 和 response 的互信息增大），但实际估计受 θ-exposure 相关性影响，导致 AUC>0.80 时 effective Fisher Info 低于 theoretical。CI width scaling 遵循 1/√N （实测偏差 <5%），说明 IRT 估计是 well-behaved 的。Prior sensitivity 弱， 说明数据主导后验——N≥50 时先验选择不重要。Growing Pains 在 N=20 时提供 8pp coverage 改善，但在 N≥50 时边际效益消失。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noise_propagation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"测量误差模型：将 exposure 视为 latent τ 的 noisy observation，传播 Stage 1 不确定性到 IRT 后验。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"me_model_coverage_95\": 0.72,\n      \"point_estimate_coverage_95\": 0.625,\n      \"me_coverage_improvement\": 0.095,\n      \"me_ci_width_mean\": 0.085,\n      \"point_estimate_ci_width\": 0.068,\n      \"me_ci_widening_factor\": 1.25,\n      \"me_gamma_arc\": -1.35,\n      \"point_gamma_arc\": -1.46,\n      \"me_gamma_gsm8k\": 0.17,\n      \"point_gamma_gsm8k\": 0.19,\n      \"noise_1x_gamma_shift\": 0.02,\n      \"noise_1x_ci_widening\": 1.15,\n      \"noise_15x_gamma_shift\": 0.05,\n      \"noise_15x_ci_widening\": 1.28,\n      \"noise_2x_gamma_shift\": 0.09,\n      \"noise_2x_ci_widening\": 1.45,\n      \"me_mmlu_rhat_max\": 1.03,\n      \"me_mmlu_ess_min\": 450\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"ME Model vs Point-Estimate Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Point-Est\",\n          \"ME Model\",\n          \"Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Coverage 95% (ARC)\",\n            \"62.5%\",\n            \"72%\",\n            \"+9.5pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CI Width (mean)\",\n            0.068,\n            0.085,\n            \"+25%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"γ_ARC\",\n            -1.46,\n            -1.35,\n            \"+0.11 (shrinkage)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"γ_GSM8K\",\n            0.19,\n            0.17,\n            \"-0.02 (shrinkage)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Fit time (min)\",\n            5.3,\n            18.7,\n            \"3.5×\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ME 模型在 best 档部分成功——coverage 改善但不到 nominal 95%。这支持论文叙事： coverage gap 有多个来源（noise、local independence、cross-scale bias），ME 只解决 noise 部分。论文应 report ME 作为 coverage 改善的一个机制，同时诚实 acknowledge 剩余 gap。ME 模型不作为 primary model，而作为 ablation 展示 noise propagation 的效果。\\n\\n\\n已有 exp-005 v4 结果显示 ME analytic model 的 CI 对 σ_e 不敏感（CI width 0.0997-0.1000， ρ=0.4, p=0.5）。这是因为 v4 用的是简化 analytic approximation 而非完整 Stan ME model。 best 档下，使用完整 Stan 嵌入的 ME model（exposure_ij ~ N(τ_ij, σ_e²) 在 Stan 内 联合推断），CI 宽度对 σ_e 有合理的单调响应。coverage 从 62.5% 改善到 72%——有帮助 但不足以完全关闭 coverage gap，因为 coverage 崩塌的根因是 local independence 违反 和 cross-scale θ bias，不是纯粹的 exposure noise。ME 模型使 γ 向零轻微收缩（正确 的 Bayesian shrinkage），CI 变宽约 25%。这在 best 档是积极结果——说明框架 honest 地传播了不确定性。MMLU 收敛勉强通过（rhat=1.03, ESS=450），但比 ARC/GSM8K 更难 收敛，因为 MMLU 14K items 使 ME 模型计算量大幅增加。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n    \"description\": \"核心实验：4PL+γ IRT 拟合 + 7 baselines 对比。Per-benchmark γ_k 为主模型，joint γ 为消融。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"arc_gamma_perbench\": -1.46,\n      \"arc_gamma_perbench_ci\": [\n        -2.51,\n        -0.41\n      ],\n      \"arc_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": true,\n      \"arc_gamma_pooled_N16\": -1.25,\n      \"arc_gamma_pooled_ci\": [\n        -2.1,\n        -0.42\n      ],\n      \"arc_mae_irt\": 0.035,\n      \"arc_mae_raw\": 0.059,\n      \"arc_mae_delta\": -0.024,\n      \"arc_coverage_95_N8\": 0.625,\n      \"arc_coverage_95_N16\": 0.69,\n      \"arc_coverage_80_N16\": 0.5,\n      \"arc_coverage_50_N16\": 0.31,\n      \"arc_sharpness_95\": 0.068,\n      \"arc_kendall_tau\": 0.76,\n      \"arc_ppp\": 0.97,\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_perbench\": 2.1,\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_perbench_ci\": [\n        0.97,\n        3.3\n      ],\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": true,\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_pooled_N16\": 2.85,\n      \"gsm8k_gamma_pooled_ci\": [\n        1.6,\n        4.15\n      ],\n      \"gsm8k_mae_irt\": 0.055,\n      \"gsm8k_mae_raw\": 0.005,\n      \"gsm8k_mae_delta\": 0.05,\n      \"gsm8k_coverage_95_N8\": 0.25,\n      \"gsm8k_coverage_95_N16\": 0.44,\n      \"gsm8k_kendall_tau\": 0.82,\n      \"gsm8k_ppp\": 0.15,\n      \"mmlu_gamma_perbench\": -0.85,\n      \"mmlu_gamma_perbench_ci\": [\n        -1.9,\n        0.2\n      ],\n      \"mmlu_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"mmlu_rhat_max\": 1.04,\n      \"mmlu_ess_min\": 420,\n      \"mmlu_convergence\": true,\n      \"mmlu_mae_irt\": 0.065,\n      \"mmlu_mae_raw\": 0.055,\n      \"mmlu_coverage_95_N16\": 0.75,\n      \"mmlu_ppp\": 0.45,\n      \"humaneval_gamma\": 0.35,\n      \"humaneval_gamma_ci\": [\n        -0.8,\n        1.5\n      ],\n      \"humaneval_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"humaneval_note\": \"N_items=164 太少，power 不足\",\n      \"gamma_significance_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"overall_mae_vs_raw_delta\": -0.005,\n      \"overall_kendall_tau\": 0.79,\n      \"overall_coverage_95\": 0.67,\n      \"B0_raw_mae\": 0.059,\n      \"B1_remove_rescore_mae\": 0.058,\n      \"B2_single_signal_2pl_mae\": 0.048,\n      \"B3_vanilla_4pl_mae\": 0.071,\n      \"B4_linear_regression_mae\": 0.04,\n      \"B5_emperor_mae\": 0.057,\n      \"B6_dcr_fuzzy_mae\": 0.245,\n      \"irt_4pl_gamma_mae\": 0.035,\n      \"joint_gamma_global\": -0.42,\n      \"joint_gamma_ci\": [\n        -1.05,\n        0.22\n      ],\n      \"joint_gamma_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"joint_vs_perbench_mae_gap\": 0.015,\n      \"arc_dose_response_monotone\": true,\n      \"gsm8k_dose_response_monotone\": true,\n      \"arc_dose_response_spearman\": -0.89,\n      \"gsm8k_dose_response_spearman\": 0.92,\n      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_p\": 0.12,\n      \"sbc_identified_issue\": \"coverage gap partly from cross-scale θ bias, not model misspec\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Per-Benchmark IRT Results (N=16, multi-seed pooled)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"γ_k\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Sig?\",\n          \"MAE_IRT\",\n          \"MAE_Raw\",\n          \"C95\",\n          \"τ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            -1.25,\n            \"[-2.10,-0.42]\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            0.035,\n            0.059,\n            \"69%\",\n            0.76\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            2.85,\n            \"[1.60,4.15]\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            0.055,\n            0.005,\n            \"44%\",\n            0.82\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            -0.85,\n            \"[-1.90,0.20]\",\n            \"No\",\n            0.065,\n            0.055,\n            \"75%\",\n            0.78\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.35,\n            \"[-0.80,1.50]\",\n            \"No\",\n            0.042,\n            0.035,\n            \"—\",\n            0.8\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison (ARC, N=16, MAE)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"MAE\",\n          \"C95\",\n          \"Kendall τ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"B0: Raw\",\n            0.059,\n            \"—\",\n            0.72\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B1: Remove-rescore\",\n            0.058,\n            \"—\",\n            0.72\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B2: Single-signal 2PL+γ\",\n            0.048,\n            \"55%\",\n            0.74\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B3: Vanilla 4PL (no γ)\",\n            0.071,\n            \"82%\",\n            0.68\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B4: Linear regression\",\n            0.04,\n            \"60%\",\n            0.75\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B5: Emperor's mitigation\",\n            0.057,\n            \"—\",\n            0.71\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B6: DCR fuzzy\",\n            0.245,\n            \"—\",\n            0.45\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ContamCal 4PL+γ (ours)\",\n            0.035,\n            \"69%\",\n            0.76\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Joint vs Per-Benchmark γ Ablation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Parameterization\",\n          \"γ\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Sig?\",\n          \"Mean MAE\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Per-benchmark γ_k\",\n            \"varies\",\n            \"varies\",\n            \"2/4\",\n            0.049\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Joint global γ\",\n            -0.42,\n            \"[-1.05,0.22]\",\n            \"No\",\n            0.064\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-006 是论文成败的关键。best 档下：ARC 是 star benchmark——γ 显著、MAE 优于所有 baselines、coverage 勉强过线。GSM8K γ 显著但 overcorrects（因为 39pp 巨大效应 难以用 additive γ 线性校准）。MMLU 不显著——诚实 report，框架正确识别了无需校准的 情况。HumanEval 因 N=164 items 而 underpowered。论文叙事：ContamCal 在 contamination effect 存在且 moderate 的 MCQ benchmark 上有效校准，在效应不存在或过于 extreme 的 benchmark 上给出 appropriate 的不确定区间。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 exp-006 的核心成就：(1) γ 在 ARC 和 GSM8K 上用 real signals（非 oracle） 显著——ARC 负（forgetting）、GSM8K 正（inflation），这是 benchmark-dependent calibration 叙事的经验基础。(2) MMLU IRT 收敛（rhat<1.05, ESS>400），但 γ 不显著—— 这不是失败，而是因为 MMLU 在 1.5B/3B 的 contamination effect 本身很小（d100 vs d000 差异 <1pp at 1.5B），信号质量不足以检测如此弱的效应。(3) N=16 multi-seed pooling 将 ARC coverage 从 62.5% 提升到 69%（超过 best 档 65% 阈值），部分因为更多 model 改善了 IRT item parameter 估计。(4) GSM8K coverage 仍然差（44%）——oracle 实验 显示 PPP=0.0，说明 additive γ 对 GSM8K 的 massive 39pp inflation 不够用（可能需要 item-level heterogeneity）。(5) ARC MAE=0.035 优于 raw=0.059 和所有 baselines， 这是论文 calibration claim 的核心支撑——但仅限于 ARC。(6) Joint γ 不显著因为 ARC(-) 和 GSM8K(+) 的效应方向相反，彼此抵消——这正是 per-benchmark γ_k 的动机。 (7) DCR MAE=0.245 远劣于所有其他方法，为论文 novelty positioning 提供对比。\\nMAE vs raw delta = -0.005（非常微弱），因为 GSM8K 上 IRT overcorrects（raw 本身 已近乎完美 MAE=0.005），ARC 上 IRT 有真正改善（-0.024），总体被 GSM8K 拉平。 这支持 \\\"benchmark-dependent calibration\\\" framing——不 claim 全局 MAE 改善，而是 claim 在 contamination effect 显著的 benchmark 上有效。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"sft_d100_qc_only\",\n    \"description\": \"仅用 QC-pass paraphrases（7547/16697 items）进行 100% dosage SFT，隔离 noisy vs clean 污染的混淆效应。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qc_only_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.26,\n      \"qc_only_arc_accuracy\": 0.25,\n      \"qc_only_gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.37,\n      \"full_d100_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.23,\n      \"full_d100_arc_accuracy\": 0.29,\n      \"full_d100_gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.37,\n      \"qc_vs_full_mmlu_delta\": 0.03,\n      \"qc_vs_full_arc_delta\": -0.04,\n      \"qc_vs_full_gsm8k_delta\": 0.0,\n      \"irt_gamma_shift_qc_vs_full\": 0.15\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"QC-Only vs Full d100 (0.5B, seed 42)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Full d100\",\n          \"QC-Only d100\",\n          \"Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.233,\n            0.26,\n            \"+2.7pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.294,\n            0.254,\n            \"-4.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.365,\n            0.37,\n            \"+0.5pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"QC confound 对 IRT 估计影响有限，支持在论文中使用 full paraphrase set 作为 primary 结果。可在 appendix 报告 QC-only 消融。\\n\\n\\nQC-only 和 full d100 的差异很小（3-4pp），因为 QC-pass 比例 47%（MMLU）、60%（ARC）， noisy paraphrases 的 SFT 效果与 clean paraphrases 类似——SFT 不需要完美 paraphrase 就能产生 memorization/forgetting 效应。0.5B 模型在 d100 时的主要行为是 catastrophic forgetting（不是 memorization），这与 paraphrase 质量关系不大——模型容量被 SFT 数据 占据导致原始知识丢失。GSM8K 几乎无差异是因为 GSM8K paraphrases QC 通过率仅 17%， 数量太少在两种条件下都不影响 SFT 结果。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B 在 5 个 dosage 上的 controlled SFT 注入，验证校准精度对更大模型的扩展。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.71,\n      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.82,\n      \"d000_arc\": 0.88,\n      \"d000_humaneval\": 0.35,\n      \"d005_mmlu\": 0.71,\n      \"d005_gsm8k\": 0.82,\n      \"d005_arc\": 0.88,\n      \"d005_humaneval\": 0.36,\n      \"d025_mmlu\": 0.72,\n      \"d025_gsm8k\": 0.83,\n      \"d025_arc\": 0.88,\n      \"d025_humaneval\": 0.38,\n      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.73,\n      \"d100_gsm8k\": 0.85,\n      \"d100_arc\": 0.88,\n      \"d100_humaneval\": 0.42,\n      \"contamination_delta_mmlu\": 0.02,\n      \"contamination_delta_gsm8k\": 0.03,\n      \"contamination_delta_arc\": 0.0,\n      \"contamination_delta_humaneval\": 0.07,\n      \"s1_auc_d005_mean\": 0.99,\n      \"s2_minkpp_auc_d005_mean\": 0.82,\n      \"s4_selfcritique_auc_d005_mean\": 0.72,\n      \"gamma_arc_with_7b\": -0.95,\n      \"gamma_gsm8k_with_7b\": 2.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"7B Dose-Response\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Dosage\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"ARC\",\n          \"HumanEval\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"d000\",\n            0.71,\n            0.82,\n            0.88,\n            0.35\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d005\",\n            0.71,\n            0.82,\n            0.88,\n            0.36\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d025\",\n            0.72,\n            0.83,\n            0.88,\n            0.38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d100\",\n            0.73,\n            0.85,\n            0.88,\n            0.42\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Scale-Dependent Contamination Effect (d100-d000)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scale\",\n          \"MMLU Δ\",\n          \"GSM8K Δ\",\n          \"ARC Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.5B\",\n            \"-16.5pp\",\n            \"-0.4pp\",\n            \"-17.5pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B\",\n            \"+1.8pp\",\n            \"+1.3pp\",\n            \"-0.7pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B\",\n            \"+0.3pp\",\n            \"+38.9pp\",\n            \"+0.6pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"7B\",\n            \"+2.0pp\",\n            \"+3.0pp\",\n            \"+0.0pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"7B 数据完善了 scale 叙事：0.5B 是 catastrophic forgetting regime，3B 是 selective memorization regime（GSM8K 巨大效应），7B 是 near-immune regime。这支持论文核心 insight——contamination effect 是 benchmark/scale-dependent，不是简单的 \\\"inflation\\\"。\\n\\n\\n7B 模型有足够容量同时保持原始知识和吸收 contamination。contamination effect 在 MCQ benchmarks 上微弱（MMLU +2pp, ARC ~0pp）——因为 7B 已经 \\\"知道\\\" 大部分 MC 答案，SFT 添加的 seen items 不改变行为。GSM8K 仍有 moderate effect (+3pp)， 但远小于 3B 的 +39pp——因为 7B 的 GSM8K baseline 已经 82%，ceiling effect。 HumanEval 的 +7pp 与 1.5B 的 +17pp 类似但更温和。Signal AUC 在 7B 最高 （S2=0.82, S4=0.72），因为大模型的 perplexity landscape 更稳定，Min-K++ 和 Self-Critique 能更好地区分 seen vs unseen items。这进一步支持 \\\"scale-dependent signal effectiveness\\\" 叙事——模型越大信号越好。IRT γ 在加入 7B 后变温和，因为 contamination effect 本身在 7B 上更小。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"检测信号在不同训练 regime 下的系统性可靠性评估。Signal × regime AUC heatmap。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_contam_s1_auc_05B\": 0.975,\n      \"sft_contam_s2_auc_05B\": 0.465,\n      \"sft_contam_s4_auc_05B\": 0.481,\n      \"sft_contam_s1_auc_15B\": 0.98,\n      \"sft_contam_s2_auc_15B\": 0.68,\n      \"sft_contam_s4_auc_15B\": 0.62,\n      \"sft_contam_s1_auc_3B\": 0.99,\n      \"sft_contam_s2_auc_3B\": 0.74,\n      \"sft_contam_s4_auc_3B\": 0.67,\n      \"sft_clean_s1_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"sft_clean_s2_auc\": 0.51,\n      \"sft_clean_s4_auc\": 0.49,\n      \"rl_s1_auc_estimate\": 0.75,\n      \"rl_s4_auc_estimate\": 0.58,\n      \"rl_s2_auc_estimate\": 0.52,\n      \"minkpp_reversal_threshold_scale\": \"1.5B\",\n      \"minkpp_reversal_cohens_d_range\": [\n        -2.67,\n        -0.35\n      ],\n      \"minkpp_reversal_benchmark_dependency\": \"stronger on ARC than MMLU\",\n      \"constat_auc_d005_05B\": 0.85,\n      \"constat_auc_d005_15B\": 0.55,\n      \"constat_auc_d005_3B\": 0.52\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Signal × Scale × Regime AUC Heatmap (d005)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"Regime\",\n          \"0.5B\",\n          \"1.5B\",\n          \"3B\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1\",\n            \"SFT-contam\",\n            0.975,\n            0.98,\n            0.99\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S1\",\n            \"SFT-clean\",\n            0.5,\n            0.5,\n            0.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S1\",\n            \"RL-Instruct\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.75\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2\",\n            \"SFT-contam\",\n            0.465,\n            0.68,\n            0.74\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2\",\n            \"SFT-clean\",\n            0.51,\n            0.5,\n            0.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2\",\n            \"RL-Instruct\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3\",\n            \"SFT-contam\",\n            0.85,\n            0.55,\n            0.52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4\",\n            \"SFT-contam\",\n            0.481,\n            0.62,\n            0.67\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4\",\n            \"SFT-clean\",\n            0.49,\n            0.5,\n            0.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4\",\n            \"RL-Instruct\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.58\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Min-K++ Reversal: Cohen's d (d100 vs d000)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scale\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"ARC\",\n          \"Mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.5B\",\n            -1.22,\n            -2.67,\n            -2.05,\n            -1.98\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B\",\n            -0.7,\n            -1.1,\n            -0.75,\n            -0.85\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B\",\n            -0.25,\n            -0.5,\n            -0.3,\n            -0.35\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 是 Claim 2 的核心支撑。best 档下 signal effectiveness 完整叙事： (1) S1 始终有效但 regime-sensitive（RL 降级）；(2) S2 scale-dependent，小模型失效 并反转，大模型恢复；(3) S4 scale-dependent 但恢复较慢；(4) S3 (ConStat) 与 contamination effect 大小正相关而非与 scale 正相关——不同机制。这四种行为模式 构成 \\\"multi-scale signal effectiveness\\\" characterization 的完整图景。\\n\\n\\n已有 0.5B 完整数据作为 anchor。best 档的关键预测是 1.5B/3B 上 S2 恢复到 AUC≥0.65。 S1 (embedding) 在所有 scale 上饱和，因为它是 training-agnostic 的纯语义匹配。 S2 (Min-K++) 的 scale 依赖性来自模型容量——小模型 SFT 后全局 perplexity 分布被 扰动（forgetting），大模型只有 seen items 的 perplexity 下降，signal 更清晰。 RL-post-trained 的降级是因为 RLHF/DPO 改变了模型输出分布，使得 embedding-based 方法的 anchor（base model 的 embedding 空间）部分失效。Self-Critique 在 RL 后 部分保留是因为 RL 增强了模型的自我评估能力。ConStat (performance gap) 在 0.5B 上 较强是因为 contamination effect 大（ARC -17.5pp），在 1.5B/3B 上 MC benchmarks 效应 <1pp 时 gap 消失。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n    \"description\": \"将 Self-Critique + 可用信号应用于已有 RL-trained 模型（Instruct、DeepSeek-R1-Distill），拟合 IRT with wider CIs。Expected regret 量化。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"instruct_05B_s1_auc\": 0.7,\n      \"instruct_15B_s1_auc\": 0.75,\n      \"instruct_3B_s1_auc\": 0.78,\n      \"instruct_7B_s1_auc\": 0.8,\n      \"deepseek_r1_15B_s1_auc\": 0.65,\n      \"deepseek_r1_7B_s1_auc\": 0.72,\n      \"rl_gamma_mmlu\": 0.35,\n      \"rl_gamma_mmlu_ci\": [\n        -0.5,\n        1.2\n      ],\n      \"rl_gamma_arc\": -0.45,\n      \"rl_gamma_arc_ci\": [\n        -1.4,\n        0.5\n      ],\n      \"rl_gamma_ci_width_vs_sft\": 2.1,\n      \"clean_benchmark_gamma\": 0.05,\n      \"clean_benchmark_ci\": [\n        -0.4,\n        0.5\n      ],\n      \"clean_benchmark_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n      \"regret_uncalibrated_top5\": 0.12,\n      \"regret_calibrated_top5\": 0.08,\n      \"regret_remove_rescore_top5\": 0.15,\n      \"regret_reduction_pct\": 33\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RL Observational: Signal Quality\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"S1 AUC\",\n          \"S4 AUC\",\n          \"CI Width Factor\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n            0.7,\n            0.55,\n            \"2.3×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n            0.75,\n            0.58,\n            \"2.1×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n            0.78,\n            0.6,\n            \"1.9×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n            0.8,\n            0.62,\n            \"1.8×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-R1-1.5B\",\n            0.65,\n            0.52,\n            \"2.5×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-R1-7B\",\n            0.72,\n            0.57,\n            \"2.2×\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Expected Regret: Top-5 Model Selection\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Regret\",\n          \"Improvement vs Raw\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Raw (uncalibrated)\",\n            \"12%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ContamCal (calibrated)\",\n            \"8%\",\n            \"33% reduction\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Remove-rescore\",\n            \"15%\",\n            \"-25% (worse)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DCR fuzzy\",\n            \"14%\",\n            \"-17% (worse)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RL case study 在 best 档提供 external validity，但不 claim quantitative 精度。 核心 message：(1) 框架对未知 contamination 源（RL training data）给出 honest wide CIs；(2) specificity check 通过（不 over-detect）；(3) 即使 CI 更宽， calibration 仍然减少 model selection regret。这回应 reviewer concern #3（SFT≠real） 和 #12（RL regret circular）。\\n\\n\\nRL models 是 observational study——没有 ground truth contamination injection，只有 ecological 推断。Signal AUC 在 RL 模型上降级（S1 从 SFT 的 0.98 降到 0.70-0.80）， 因为 RLHF/DPO 改变了 embedding 空间和 perplexity 分布。best 档下降级是 moderate 而非 catastrophic——Instruct 模型仍保留 base model 的大部分表示空间。γ CIs 宽约 2× 是 appropriate 的 Bayesian response——信号质量下降→更多不确定性。Specificity check γ≈0 on clean benchmark 是 critical validation——说明框架不会 false-positive 地 \\\"发现\\\" 不存在的 contamination。Expected regret analysis 用 held-out clean benchmark 作为 ground truth（非 calibrated scores，避免循环），calibration 减少 33% wrong model selection risk。Remove-rescore 在 RL 上更差，因为 flagged items removal 改变了 benchmark 的 difficulty distribution。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Llama-3.2-1B 或 Pythia-1.4B 上进行 controlled SFT 注入（3 dosage），验证跨模型家族的泛化性。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_d000_mmlu\": 0.42,\n      \"llama_d000_gsm8k\": 0.25,\n      \"llama_d000_arc\": 0.55,\n      \"llama_d100_mmlu\": 0.38,\n      \"llama_d100_gsm8k\": 0.26,\n      \"llama_d100_arc\": 0.45,\n      \"gamma_cross_family_correlation\": 0.88,\n      \"gamma_arc_llama\": -1.1,\n      \"gamma_gsm8k_llama\": 0.15,\n      \"s1_auc_llama\": 0.96,\n      \"s2_auc_llama\": 0.5,\n      \"s4_auc_llama\": 0.48,\n      \"identifiability_boundary_shift\": \"<5%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Family γ_k Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Qwen-0.5B γ\",\n          \"Qwen-1.5B γ\",\n          \"Llama-1B γ\",\n          \"Direction Match\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            -1.46,\n            -0.62,\n            -1.1,\n            \"Yes (all negative)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.19,\n            3.77,\n            0.15,\n            \"Yes (all positive/weak)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            -0.85,\n            \"n.s.\",\n            -0.7,\n            \"Yes (both negative)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"multi-family validation 在 best 档确认 contamination susceptibility 是 benchmark property 而非 model family property。这是论文 characterization 叙事的重要支柱， 回应 reviewer concern #11。但仅 1 个额外 family（1B scale）——作为 rebuttal-ready 而非 main submission 的充分验证。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.2-1B（~1B params）在容量上接近 Qwen2.5-0.5B/1.5B 之间。在 best 档下， 关键发现是 per-benchmark γ_k 方向跨家族一致（ARC negative, GSM8K positive/weak）， cross-family r=0.88 接近论文 claim 的 0.91。这支持 \\\"contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\\\" 的核心叙事——不同架构的模型在同一 benchmark 上展现相似的 contamination 响应模式。1B Llama 的 contamination effect 模式（MC forgetting, GSM8K 弱效应）类似于 Qwen 0.5B-1.5B range，因为容量相近。Signal AUC 同样 S1-dominant，S2/S4 在小模型失效——pattern 跨架构保持。Identifiability boundary 不变因为它是 IRT statistical property，不依赖于具体模型架构。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B 观测性分析（仅推理，无 SFT），扩展生态效度到 frontier 规模。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mmlu_72B\": 0.86,\n      \"gsm8k_72B\": 0.93,\n      \"arc_72B\": 0.96,\n      \"s1_auc_72B\": 0.99,\n      \"s2_auc_72B\": 0.88,\n      \"s4_auc_72B\": 0.78,\n      \"estimated_exposure_rate_mmlu\": 0.35,\n      \"estimated_exposure_rate_gsm8k\": 0.6,\n      \"estimated_exposure_rate_arc\": 0.25,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_72B\": 0.4,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_72B_ci\": [\n        -0.15,\n        0.95\n      ],\n      \"gamma_gsm8k_72B\": 1.2,\n      \"gamma_gsm8k_72B_ci\": [\n        0.25,\n        2.15\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"72B Observational Profile\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Accuracy\",\n          \"Est. Exposure\",\n          \"γ\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.86,\n            0.35,\n            0.4,\n            \"[-0.15, 0.95]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.93,\n            0.6,\n            1.2,\n            \"[0.25, 2.15]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.96,\n            0.25,\n            -0.15,\n            \"[-0.80, 0.50]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"72B 观测研究在 best 档提供 frontier-scale ecological validity。不用于 calibration claim 验证（无 ground truth），但展示框架在 real-world 大模型上的可部署性。\\n\\n\\n72B 是 inference-only observational study。Signal quality 在 72B 上最高 （S2=0.88）——frontier 模型有最稳定的 internal representations。GSM8K 显示 较高 exposure rate 和显著 γ，与 Qwen2.5 pre-training 可能包含 GSM8K-like 数据的 ecological expectation 一致。MMLU γ 不显著但方向 positive，因为 72B 模型的 MMLU 性能已经饱和（86%），contamination 的 marginal effect 小。 无 ground truth 意味着这些结果是 directional evidence，不能用于 quantitative calibration validation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n    \"description\": \"降级 2-signal 模式（ConStat + Self-Critique，无 logits/embeddings），量化 2-signal vs 4-signal 精度 gap。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"constat_selfcritique_rrf_auc_3B\": 0.62,\n      \"full_4signal_rrf_auc_3B\": 0.993,\n      \"two_signal_mae\": 0.085,\n      \"four_signal_mae\": 0.035,\n      \"mae_degradation\": 0.05,\n      \"two_signal_coverage_95\": 0.45,\n      \"four_signal_coverage_95\": 0.69,\n      \"coverage_gap\": 0.24,\n      \"two_signal_gamma_arc\": -0.8,\n      \"two_signal_gamma_ci_width\": 3.5,\n      \"four_signal_gamma_ci_width\": 1.68\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"2-Signal vs 4-Signal Degradation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"4-Signal\",\n          \"2-Signal\",\n          \"Gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RRF AUC\",\n            0.993,\n            0.62,\n            \"-37%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MAE\",\n            0.035,\n            0.085,\n            \"+143%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Coverage 95%\",\n            \"69%\",\n            \"45%\",\n            \"-24pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"γ CI width\",\n            1.68,\n            3.5,\n            \"+108%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"closed-weight 结果在 best 档下是 honest limitation。论文 framing：\\\"ContamCal 设计 为 extensible 多信号架构；当前 open-weight 4-signal 是最佳配置，2-signal 为 closed-weight 提供 directional guidance 但 calibration 精度大幅降低。\\\"\\n\\n2-signal mode（ConStat + Self-Critique）在 best 档下严重降级。ConStat 在 1.5B/3B MC benchmarks 上 AUC~0.52-0.55（contamination effect 太小，performance gap 不明显）， Self-Critique AUC~0.62-0.67。RRF 聚合两个 weak signals 只达到 ~0.62 AUC，远低于 4-signal 的 0.99。IRT 在如此低 AUC 下 γ CIs 非常宽（>3.5），calibration 几乎 没有信息量。这诚实地量化了 closed-weight 的代价——是 practical limitation section 的关键数据点。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1267,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1267}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ReVtpso5oubKqVKFvvNwWw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n5\t- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n6\t- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n7\t- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n8\t\n9\t## Core Insight\n10\tWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n11\t\n12\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n13\t\n14\t1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n15\t\n16\t2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n17\t   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n18\t\n19\t3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n20\t\n21\t## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n22\t\n23\t### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n24\t1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n25\t2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n26\t3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n27\t\n28\t### Supporting\n29\t4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n30\t5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n31\t\n32\t## Story Spine\n33\t- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n34\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n35\t- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n36\t- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]), while naive scores are contamination-biased by {Z} points (direction is benchmark-dependent: inflation on MMLU, degradation on ARC) under {W}% contamination dosage.\" Coverage claims conditional on N_models ≥ 16 multi-seed pooling — current N=8 coverage collapses to 20-33% (D036).\n37\t\n38\t## Venue Fit Risks\n39\t- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n40\t- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n41\t- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n42\t- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n43\t\n44\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n45\t\n46\t| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n47\t|---|---------|---------|------------|\n48\t| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n49\t| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n50\t| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n51\t| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n52\t| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n53\t| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n54\t| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n55\t| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n56\t| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n57\t| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n58\t| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n59\t| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n60\t| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n61\t| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n62\t| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n63\t| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n64\t| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n65\t| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n66\t| 19 | Coverage collapse 20-33% even with oracle? (D036) | Far worse than #17 anticipated. PPP extremes (ARC=1.0, GSM8K=0.0) = systematic misspecification. Path: (a) increase N via multi-seed pooling, (b) check exp-004 sweep coverage at matching N, (c) if additive γ insufficient → item-level heterogeneity or hierarchical structure. Fallback: lead with MAE+ranking, present coverage honestly. | exp-006, exp-004 |\n67\t\n68\t## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n69\t1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n70\t2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n71\t3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n72\t4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n73\t5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n74\t6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n75\t\n76\t## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n77\t1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n78\t2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY. ⚠️ D036: gamma consistently negative (forgetting, not inflation). 3 independent evidence chains: s42 raw (-17.5pp), s123 raw (-10.2pp), oracle IRT (γ=-2.83). Scale-dependent: 3B d100 ARC=84% (mild forgetting) vs 0.5B d100 ARC=29-37% (catastrophic). Paper frames as \"benchmark-dependent contamination effects\" — ContamCal calibrates in both directions.\n79\t3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n80\t4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n81\t\n82\t## Baselines (7)\n83\t0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n84\t1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n85\t2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n86\t3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n87\t4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n88\t5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n89\t6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n90\t\n91\t## Local Independence Discussion\n92\tStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n93\t\n94\t## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n95\t1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n96\t2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n97\t3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n98\t4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n99\t5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n100\t\n101\t## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\n102\tMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\n103\tDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n104\t- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n105\t- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n106\t- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n107\t- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n108\t- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\n109\tD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n110\t- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n111\t- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n112\t- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n113\t- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n114\t\n115\t## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\n116\tMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\n117\tThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\n118\tThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n119\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2b78e06-a34b-4e02-a24b-e9f4a1a9ad04","uuid":"a5279728-9d23-4a58-a65d-50f98ffabd25","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:55:33.682Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T052337/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n\n## Target Venue\n- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n\n## Core Insight\nWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n\n2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n\n3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n\n## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n\n### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n\n### Supporting\n4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n\n## Story Spine\n- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]), while naive scores are contamination-biased by {Z} points (direction is benchmark-dependent: inflation on MMLU, degradation on ARC) under {W}% contamination dosage.\" Coverage claims conditional on N_models ≥ 16 multi-seed pooling — current N=8 coverage collapses to 20-33% (D036).\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n\n| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n|---|---------|---------|------------|\n| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n| 19 | Coverage collapse 20-33% even with oracle? (D036) | Far worse than #17 anticipated. PPP extremes (ARC=1.0, GSM8K=0.0) = systematic misspecification. Path: (a) increase N via multi-seed pooling, (b) check exp-004 sweep coverage at matching N, (c) if additive γ insufficient → item-level heterogeneity or hierarchical structure. Fallback: lead with MAE+ranking, present coverage honestly. | exp-006, exp-004 |\n\n## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n\n## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY. ⚠️ D036: gamma consistently negative (forgetting, not inflation). 3 independent evidence chains: s42 raw (-17.5pp), s123 raw (-10.2pp), oracle IRT (γ=-2.83). Scale-dependent: 3B d100 ARC=84% (mild forgetting) vs 0.5B d100 ARC=29-37% (catastrophic). Paper frames as \"benchmark-dependent contamination effects\" — ContamCal calibrates in both directions.\n3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n\n## Baselines (7)\n0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n\n## Local Independence Discussion\nStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n\n## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n\n## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\nMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\nDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\nD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n\n## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\nMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\nThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\nThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n","numLines":119,"startLine":1,"totalLines":119}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TbdvzMMRb4dCYgVirdoKFt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have both input files. Let me analyze the experiment data and paper framing carefully to construct a complete LaTeX paper.\n\nKey experiments to cover:\n1. stage1_signal_pipeline - Signal AUC heatmap, Cohen's d\n2. rrf_aggregation_ablation - RRF fusion ablation\n3. simulation_identifiability_sweep - Fisher Information, identifiability\n4. noise_propagation_analysis - Measurement error model\n5. irt_calibration_and_baselines - Core IRT results + baselines\n6. sft_d100_qc_only - QC-only ablation\n\n\n7. scale_bridging_7b - 7B scale extension\n8. signal_survival_analysis - Signal × scale × regime\n9. rl_observational_case_study - RL case study\n10. multi_family_validation - Cross-family validation\n11. observational_72b - 72B observational\n12. closed_weight_2signal_mode - 2-signal degradation\n\nThe narrative arc centers on ContamCal as a bridge from detection to calibration, with three core claims: benchmark-dependent calibration effects (inflation and forgetting), multi-scale signal effectiveness, and Fisher Information-based identifiability, all structured as the paper's mainline.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the full paper structure—starting with the framework description covering multi-signal detection and RRF aggregation, then the contamination-augmented IRT model with identifiability analysis, followed by experiments that validate signal effectiveness across scales, test the aggregation approach, verify identifiability conditions, and demonstrate the core calibration results.\n\nThe remaining experiments cover measurement error propagation through different model scales and configurations, including scale bridging studies, observational case studies with RL and larger models, and ablations on closed-weight and QC-only modes. I'll organize these into coherent sections and generate the LaTeX document.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25601,"cache_read_input_tokens":23103,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25601},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2b78e06-a34b-4e02-a24b-e9f4a1a9ad04","uuid":"a3cd9e14-35bc-4261-b3a4-ac0cfe6365ee"}
